"test:rules derives the metamodel`s rules over one literal store with derive over derive:rp_rules. Its Fact joins Fact rows are held under the metamodel`s own names (instances.md:234-240, core.md:580-588, 686): fa fills ra1 and ra2, fb fills rb1 and rb2, rows of Fact fills Role, the fact type RoleInstance its objectification names; each RoleInstance, keyed by its fact and role joined with a period as an objectified instance is (rmap:proj_objkey), uses an Object Type Instance: fa.ra1 va, fa.ra2 vb, fb.rb1 vb, fb.rb2 vc; ra1 and ra2 are used in Reading rda, rb1 and rb2 in rdb, at Positions 1 and 2, held as the text the reader files a Position as (ra1.rda 1, ra2.rda 2, rb1.rdb 1, rb2.rdb 2). So fa`s position-2 role uses vb, which fb`s position-1 role uses, and fa joins fb (core.md:1585); nothing else joins. The rows were FactFillsRoleUsesResource, keyed by a nested <fact, role>, and a nested RoleIsUsedInReadingHasPosition: the ternary the nesting retired and a name the Resource rename retired.",
