"THE STORE-WIDE INDUCTION IS OUT OF THE REPORT. test:induce's first conjunct applied induce to every declared derived fact type of the store under test, rebuilding candidate rules from every pair of the store's binary fact types and checking that their union covered each declared population -- 3.18 million induce:join_cands calls in the first 90 s of a large app's report over its compiled map, the whole of that report's cost once the map was compiled. Nothing in the by-hand process does that: a derivation is declared and the report checks that the declared rule evaluates to its population (test:derive, the step-product laws) and that the map agrees with NORMA. The induce function keeps its fixtures below, which are its test, and stays the cli's induce action; the report no longer runs it over the store, and induce:declared, the declared derived fact types that conjunct alone read, went with it (the unreachable-set law named it).",

