"AND A FUNCTION THE MODEL CANNOT FULLY ADDRESS IS A CALL NOBODY CAN MAKE. test:callable holds when every Function backed by a Federation has a method, a system with a URL, and a path. It is VACUOUS on a store that federates with nothing -- the base store -- so it costs nothing there, and it is the detector for a Function like sendSupportEmail with its system, its URL and its path and NO METHOD, which nothing else reports. The headers are not checked here because whether a call needs one is the Federation's business, not the Function's; that is a second law over FederationAuthenticatesWithHeader and it is owed.",
"AND IT IS OF THE FUNCTIONS CALLED OVER THE BOUNDARY. The reflection`s Connector is backed by the Federation `lambda` (federation.md) and is fetched by a compiled Fetcher, not called with a method at a URL, so a Function backed by a compiled Federation (fed:compiled) is not one of the rows. UNCHECKED: never run.",
