          S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1)))))),
"AND FILE HOLDS THE POPULATION, NOT ONLY THE SOURCE. This law held each descriptor`s rows within the population system:pop_rows reads, and never read FILE, which a GET`s links are made from (nav:peers) and which system:pop_in reads where a fact type has no cell of its own. So a population put by name and never refiled went unseen, and a write`s closure left FILE`s cell of every derived fact type it moved as it was. test:fip_cell holds FILE`s cell of a declared fact type, unnested, to be the rows system:pop_rows reads, as a set; a fact type FILE has no cell for reads as none. On this alone the law answered F, and its witness named 29 declared fact types of the composed base store, each a population the start`s reflection or closure had put. Operand <store, descriptor>.",
"AND A DERIVED FACT TYPE THE STORE COMPUTES ON READ HAS NOTHING IN FILE: FILE holds what the store keeps, and such a derived fact type is kept nowhere, so its cell is absent or empty, while system:pop_rows computes it.",
