          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))), K(A("#")))), K(PHI()), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:unnest"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))), K(A("#")))), K(A("T")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:unnest"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))))))),
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))), K(A("#")))), K(PHI()), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:unnest"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(1)))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1)))))))),
"AND OVER A STORE SERVED FROM ITS DATABASE, FILE IS THE DATABASE, AND IT IS HELD TO THE LEDGERS. A store booted from its database builds no FILE cell (main:boot: store:for_read of store:boot), so test:fip_cell read every declared fact type there as none, and the law named each one that has a population: MEASURED on Java over the base store compile-store wrote, 102 fact types, and none over the carriers. FILE there is the tables, and what they must hold is what the compile says they hold: its ledgers, _readings (the facts the readings assert) and _derived (those its closure added), which it writes beside the tables and no read moves. So a fact type the database places (test:fip_placed: store:sql_place is a place) is held to them: test:fip_ledger <store, descriptor> is T when the rows the ledgers hold of it (sqlite:ledger_one) are, as a set, the rows a reader reads at its place (system:pop_rows), each spelled as the ledgers spell it (compile:json_val). A fact type no table places, and every fact type of a store held in memory, is read as before.",
