          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:sup_meet"))))),
"AND THE PAGE HOST`S ENTRY IS AN ENTRY. tools/js-runner/page.js, the host an artifact page runs, applies main for the page it writes and artifact:follow for each link the page follows, so artifact:follow is listed with the other hosts` entries and what it calls, artifact:writes and ui:write, is reached from it.",
"AND THE EMIT`S DDL IS AN ENTRY. The js host`s emitToDb applies schema:emit_ddl to the store before a write, the store after it and the store`s database, and test:dc_remap, which named it, asks the database the law lays out instead (test:dr_emit), so schema:emit_ddl is listed with the hosts` entries.",
"AND SO IS THE EMIT`S REFLECTION. emitToDb applies reflect:write_steps before its transaction and reflect:sql_adopt after it, and no host reflects a store in memory any more, so store:reflect_pass is reached from store:close alone and store:reflect_since from nothing.",
"AND SO ARE THE WRITE`S CHECKS IN SQL. emitToDb applies delta:write_steps before its transaction, and the boot applies delta:boot_cover to the store`s database, so both are listed with the hosts` entries. AND THE REFUSAL ITS CHECKS DENY, AND THE REFRESH: storeAnswer applies delta:refused to the denied checks` rows, and the boot applies delta:boot_refresh to the store`s database.",
"AND SO IS WHETHER THE STORE MOVED. The serving tails apply store:version at the start and store:freshen to the store before each request (storeFreshen), and store:commit_note at each commit a write lambda runs makes to the store they serve (commitNoted), so they are listed with the hosts` entries, and store:stale with them.",
