    S5(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:thm2_at")), A("distl"),
       S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:thm2_addrs")))),
"test:thm2 asks every link of every entity of one store, and each on-read derived fact type a link reads asks derive:or_dfts of that store; it is a value of the store, which the test does not change, so the store carries it (state:or_dfts, store:boot_cell) as a store booted to serve does, and every link reads it; and so for store:fts (state:fts_boot), which store:fts_cached holds to the store`s own state:fts.",
"test:or_plays_declared: an on-read derived fact type`s candidate players are the ones its reading declares. Domain reaches Domain is played by Domain twice, and Domain is a subtype of Function, which its descriptor is collapsed to; main:or_plays answers Domain and Domain.",
DEF("test:or_plays_declared",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("main:or_plays"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(A("DomainReachesDomain"))), A("test:read_store"))),
          K(S1(S2(A("DomainReachesDomain"), S2(A("Domain"), A("Domain")))))))),
DEF("test:thm2",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:thm2_proj"), A("test:thm2_union")), A("test:read_store"))),

"COROLLARY 3 (cor:hier, THE VIEW HIERARCHY) WAS BUILT IN FULL AND WATCHED BY NOTHING. ui:hier, ui:rank, ui:sub, ui:top and ui:schemascreen each had exactly one caller and not one of them was a law, so the computation the corollary calls `the whole view hierarchy ... with no hand-written map` could be edited into nonsense and every gate would pass. The corollary makes three statements and this holds all three. RANKED: iterated removal of parentless entity types ranks EVERY type, so the names ui:rank answers are the groups, each exactly once -- a type dropped from the ranking is a view with no place in the hierarchy. TOP: `the initial representation is the collections of rank 0`, so the rank-0 names are exactly ui:top, the groups that are nobody's child. EDGES: removal takes a type only once its parents are gone, so every child relation edge runs from a rank to a rank no higher, `types on a cycle of the child relation sharing the rank at which removal stalls` being the equal case -- measured on a large app's store, 49 of 127 edges strict and 78 equal, the stall bucket. What the corollary says beyond this -- that a collection descends to its entities and an entity descends by links(e) -- is held in test:thm2_union, which walks exactly that descent.",
