"AND A FUNCTION DELIVERS WHAT IT YIELDS (an externally federated fact is a derivation of some kind). A fact type a Source`s Function yields is derived by that Function, so a derived fact type marked for it is delivered though no rule sentence names it: test:marker_undelivered is the marked derived fact types less those a rule delivers and those a Function yields (fed:yielded_fts). Operand: the store.",
DEF("test:marker_undelivered",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:marker_marked"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:marker_dfts"), A("fed:yielded_fts")))))),
DEF("test:markers_witness",
    S3(A("CONS"), A("test:marker_undelivered"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:marker_dfts"), A("test:marker_known"))))),
DEF("test:markers",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("null")), A("test:markers_witness"))),

