       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), K(A("\"<refused>\"")))), K(PHI()),
          S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("quote_str"), A("main:case_text"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("case")), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)))), K(PHI()),
             S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))))))),
"THE ARTIFACT IS ONE MORE RENDER TARGET, AND ITS LAWS COME FIRST (an artifact is like a custom native view, to which arest data may be bound, powered through its own fact base). An artifact is a published HTML page, so its widgets are the html: realizations lambda already carries, and its layout engine is render:artifact, the Render Target readings/ui/render-target-instances.md declares, whose body is lambda`s artifact:page: one self-contained document from the panes navigate answers. test:artifact_pairs holds that the pairing covers every control kind the view emits: every kind the placed rows of a fixture entity screen carry, their children and the view`s menu among them, is a declared control, each has its html: realization in the store, and the artifact`s registration, render:<kind> for each declared control with a realization and render:artifact as its engine, leaves ui:unpaired_of nothing. test:artifact_links holds Theorem 2 of the emitted page: the hrefs the page carries, read back out of its text, are the links the entity screen carries, its transitions at its status as ui:transitions answers them over a store with a machine, Support Response r1 at Draft offered approve and redraft, and its nav item, as many as there are and no other. The nav leg is the literal shape ui:facts answers; the transitions leg is computed. Before artifact:page exists both answer F, through test:artifact_built, and not by dying. Operand of both: the composed store, which gives the declared controls; the fixture is literal.",
DEF("test:artifact_store",
    K(S(S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S1(S2(A("r1"), A("Support Response")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("StateMachineDefinitionIsForObjectType"), S1(S2(A("Support Response"), A("Support Response")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsInitialInStateMachineDefinition"), S1(S2(A("Draft"), A("Support Response")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S2(S2(A("Draft"), A("Support Response")), S2(A("Sent"), A("Support Response")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S2(S2(A("approve"), A("Support Response")), S2(A("redraft"), A("Support Response")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsFromStatus"), S2(S2(A("approve"), A("Draft")), S2(A("redraft"), A("Draft")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsToStatus"), S2(S2(A("approve"), A("Sent")), S2(A("redraft"), A("Draft")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsTriggeredByEventType"), S2(S2(A("approve"), A("AdminApprovesSupportResponse")), S2(A("redraft"), A("AdminRedraftsSupportResponse")))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("state:readings"), S1(S1(S3(A("AdminRedraftsSupportResponse"), S2(A("Admin"), A("Support Response")), S1(S3(A("{0}"), A("redrafts"), A("{1}"))))))),
        S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionHasEventLabel"), S1(S2(A("approve"), A("Approve")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminApprovesSupportResponse"), PHI()), S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminRedraftsSupportResponse"), PHI())))))),
DEF("test:artifact_nav",
    K(S1(S3(A("menu"), A("Support Response answers Support Request"), S4(A("item"), A("sr1"), A("Support Response r1 answers Support Request sr1."), S2(A("Support Request"), A("sr1"))))))),
DEF("test:artifact_layer",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("layer"), A("Support Response r1"), PHI())),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:transitions"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:artifact_store"), K(A("Support Response")), K(A("r1")))), A("test:artifact_nav")))))),
DEF("test:artifact_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:arrange"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:artifact_layer"), K(S2(N(300), PHI()))))),
DEF("test:artifact_page",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("artifact:page"), S5(A("CONS"), K(A("Support Response r1")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("detail")), A("id"))), A("test:artifact_rows")), K(PHI()), K(PHI())))),
DEF("test:artifact_built",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("artifact:page")), A("id"))))),
DEF("test:artifact_match",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), N(1)), K(A("F")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(2)))), A("theta:seteq"))))),
DEF("test:artifact_links",
    S4(A("COND"), A("test:artifact_built"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:artifact_match"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("artifact:hrefs"), A("test:artifact_page")), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("html:href")), A("artifact:links"), A("test:artifact_layer")))),
       K(A("F")))),
DEF("test:artifact_pairs",
    S4(A("COND"), A("test:artifact_built"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("artifact:kinds"), A("test:artifact_rows")), A("artifact:ctl_kinds"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("artifact:has_html")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("artifact:kinds"), A("test:artifact_rows")), A("id")))),
             S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("ui:unpaired_of"), S4(A("CONS"), A("ui:ctl_declared"), K(S1(A("render:artifact"))), A("artifact:registered"))))))),
       K(A("F")))),
"A PLATFORM OPENED AT AN ENTITY SHOWS ITS COLLECTION IN THE MASTER. An artifact page is a platform whose first navigation is the address it was published at, so its stacks are empty and its address is an entity of the store it serves. The entity went to the detail pane and the master, holding no view, drew the vanity layer, the description of whichever domain the store lists last. iFactr`s master holds the list a detail is chosen from, so a platform that registers more than one pane and is opened at an entity of an addressable type holds that type`s collection in its master and the entity at the detail`s root. test:artifact_master asks it of ui:navp over the composed store: fresh master and detail stacks and the address Function Function leave the master holding the collection Function and the detail the entity. It answered F first, the master left empty.",
DEF("test:artifact_master",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), N(2), A("ui:navp"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(S2(A("master"), PHI()), S2(A("detail"), PHI()))), K(S2(A("Function"), A("Function"))))),
       K(S2(S2(A("master"), S1(S1(A("Function")))), S2(A("detail"), S1(S2(A("Function"), A("Function"))))))))),
"AN ENTITY SCREEN SHOWS THE STATUS ITS MACHINE HOLDS IT AT. An entity of a type with a machine showed its columns, its relations and its transitions, and nowhere the status it stands at: the actions section carried it in its title, which ui:viewprops makes the title of the view`s Menu, and no widget draws a menu`s title, so an Issue at Filed read Filed nowhere on its artifact page. test:artifact_status asks it of the page: the entity screen of the fixture`s Support Response r1, ui:entity_at over test:artifact_store, arranged and written by artifact:page, carries the field ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus with the value Draft. It answered F first.",
DEF("test:artifact_status_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("apndl"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), PHI())), S3(A("COMP"), A("apndl"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:derived"), PHI())), A("test:artifact_store")))))),
DEF("test:artifact_status_page",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("artifact:page"), S5(A("CONS"), K(A("Support Response r1")),
       S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("detail")), A("id"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:arrange"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:entity_at"), S5(A("CONS"), A("test:artifact_status_store"), K(S2(A("Support Response"), A("r1"))), K(PHI()), K(A("Support Response")))), K(S2(N(300), PHI()))))),
       K(PHI()), K(PHI())))),
DEF("test:artifact_status",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("read:memberw"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus")), A("id"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("read:memberw"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Draft")), A("id"))))),
       A("fed:split"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("'")), A("test:artifact_status_page")))),
"test:recipe_sql_forms holds sqlite:recipe_sql to the served query verb on the count and cmp forms (every constraint is one SQL query). Over four literal populations -- R and S of three columns, G and K of two -- each recipe below is run twice: as the SQL sqlite:recipe_sql makes of it, in a database with no file (sqlite:scratch) holding those rows, and by query, which is derive:eval over the same rows; the two answers must be the same set of rows, each value as its text, since sqlite:scratch answers text. The recipes are count and cmp alone, nested under proj, minus and sel, over a join, and a count of a count. R holds integers, so cmp orders its columns as numbers, where 2 is less than 10 and 10 is not less than 9, as value:ge orders two integers; S holds text, ordered by its characters, where Zed is less than abc. A count is a number: sel on a count`s second column with the number 3 finds its row only if the count is one, and the column`s SQL type is integer. Run first with sqlite:recipe_sql having no arm for count or cmp, it answered F.",
"Four populations, as query reads them.",
DEF("test:rsf_pairs",
    K(S4(S2(A("R"), S5(S3(A("a"), N(1), N(5)), S3(A("b"), N(7), N(2)), S3(A("c"), N(3), N(3)), S3(A("d"), N(10), N(9)), S3(A("e"), N(2), N(10)))),
         S2(A("S"), S4(S3(A("x"), A("apple"), A("banana")), S3(A("y"), A("pear"), A("fig")), S3(A("z"), A("Zed"), A("abc")), S3(A("w"), A("fig"), A("fig")))),
         S2(A("G"), S5(S2(A("a"), A("red")), S2(A("b"), A("red")), S2(A("c"), A("blue")), S2(A("d"), A("red")), S2(A("e"), A("blue")))),
         S2(A("K"), S4(S2(A("k1"), A("a")), S2(A("k2"), A("b")), S2(A("k3"), A("c")), S2(A("k4"), A("a"))))))),
"The same populations as the script that stores them, integers as integers and text as text.",
DEF("test:rsf_script",
    K(A("create table R (c1, c2, c3); insert into R values ('a', 1, 5), ('b', 7, 2), ('c', 3, 3), ('d', 10, 9), ('e', 2, 10); create table S (c1, c2, c3); insert into S values ('x', 'apple', 'banana'), ('y', 'pear', 'fig'), ('z', 'Zed', 'abc'), ('w', 'fig', 'fig'); create table G (c1, c2); insert into G values ('a', 'red'), ('b', 'red'), ('c', 'blue'), ('d', 'red'), ('e', 'blue'); create table K (c1, c2); insert into K values ('k1', 'a'), ('k2', 'b'), ('k3', 'c'), ('k4', 'a');"))),
"Where each population is stored: its table, its columns in role order, and no flag column.",
DEF("test:rsf_places",
    K(S4(S2(A("R"), S3(A("R"), S3(A("c1"), A("c2"), A("c3")), A("#"))), S2(A("S"), S3(A("S"), S3(A("c1"), A("c2"), A("c3")), A("#"))), S2(A("G"), S3(A("G"), S2(A("c1"), A("c2")), A("#"))), S2(A("K"), S3(A("K"), S2(A("c1"), A("c2")), A("#")))))),
DEF("test:rsf_recipes",
    K(S(S3(A("count"), A("G"), N(2)),
        S3(A("count"), S3(A("proj"), A("K"), S1(N(2))), N(1)),
        S4(A("cmp"), A("R"), N(2), N(3)),
        S4(A("cmp"), A("S"), N(2), N(3)),
        S3(A("proj"), S4(A("cmp"), A("R"), N(2), N(3)), S1(N(1))),
        S3(A("minus"), S3(A("proj"), A("R"), S1(N(1))), S3(A("proj"), S4(A("cmp"), A("R"), N(2), N(3)), S1(N(1)))),
        S4(A("sel"), S3(A("count"), A("G"), N(2)), N(2), N(3)),
        S3(A("count"), S4(A("join"), A("K"), A("G"), S3(N(1), N(2), N(3))), N(3)),
        S4(A("cmp"), S4(A("join"), A("K"), A("R"), S3(N(1), N(3), N(4))), N(2), N(3)),
        S3(A("count"), S3(A("count"), A("G"), N(2)), N(2)),
        S4(A("sel"), S4(A("cmp"), A("R"), N(2), N(3)), N(1), A("e"))))),
"A recipe to the SQL sqlite:recipe_sql makes of it over the law`s places.",
DEF("test:rsf_sql",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(1), A("sqlite:recipe_sql"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:rsf_places")))),
"A recipe to the rows its SQL answers over the law`s rows.",
DEF("test:rsf_got",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:scratch"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:rsf_script"), A("test:rsf_sql"), K(PHI())))),
"A recipe to the rows the evaluator answers over the law`s populations, each value as its text.",
DEF("test:rsf_want",
    S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:flat"))), A("derive:eval"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:rsf_pairs")))),
"A recipe to T when its SQL answers what query answers; F when sqlite:recipe_sql has no arm for a form in it, whose SQL then holds its #.",
DEF("test:rsf_one",
    S4(A("COND"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("#")), A("chars")), A("test:rsf_sql")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rsf_got"), A("test:rsf_want"))))),
"T when the column a count answers is an SQL integer.",
DEF("test:rsf_typed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:scratch"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:rsf_script"), S3(A("COMP"), A("implode"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("")), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("SELECT DISTINCT typeof(c2) FROM (")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rsf_sql"), K(S3(A("count"), A("G"), N(2)))), K(A(")"))))), K(PHI()))), K(S1(S1(A("integer"))))))),
"test:sql_set_once holds that a recipe`s SQL is deduplicated once, at its top: a join over the law`s places has no DISTINCT inside it, and the SQL of a derived fact type made of it opens with the one SELECT DISTINCT. A DISTINCT subquery is never flattened into a join by SQLite, and on a large app`s store one such nesting took 343 s where the flat join takes 0.23 s. Run first, the join held three DISTINCTs; it failed. The count over a projection with a repeated value (test:rsf_recipes) holds that a count still counts a set.",
DEF("test:sql_set_once",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rsf_sql"), K(S5(A("joinon"), A("G"), A("K"), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), S4(N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4))))), K(A("DISTINCT"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(1), A("sqlite:dft_sql"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(S5(A("joinon"), A("G"), A("K"), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), S4(N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4))))), A("test:rsf_places"))), K(A("SELECT DISTINCT * FROM"))))))),
"test:ix_partial holds that an index the compile lays out on a column an entity can stand in holds only the rows with a value there: laid out from test:dl_a`s rows in a scratch database, every ix: index is partial, WHERE its column IS NOT NULL, and there is at least one.",
DEF("test:ixp_q",
    K(A("select (select count(*) from sqlite_master where type = 'index' and name like 'ix:%' and sql like '%WHERE%IS NOT NULL'), (select count(*) from sqlite_master where type = 'index' and name like 'ix:%')"))),
DEF("test:ix_partial",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), A("eq"), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("0")))))), N(1),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:scratch"), S4(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:da_script"), S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(4)), A("test:dl_cases"))), A("test:ixp_q"), K(PHI()))))),
"test:schema_fresh holds that a read sees the table a write just laid out again: in one evaluation a store gets T with one column, a read of T, T laid out again with two columns, and a read of T`s every column EXCEPT a two-column row, which answers T`s one row. A read connection kept with the first layout answered `SELECTs to the left and right of EXCEPT do not have the same number of result columns` (fails first).",
DEF("test:sf_db",
    K(A("law-schema-fresh.db"))),
DEF("test:schema_fresh",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(5), K(S1(S2(A("x"), A("y")))))),
       S7(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:fresh"), A("test:sf_db")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:exec"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sf_db"), K(A("create table t (a text); insert into t values ('x');")))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:query"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:sf_db"), K(A("select * from t")), K(PHI()))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:exec"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sf_db"), K(A("drop table t; create table t (a text, b text); insert into t values ('x', 'y');")))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:query"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:sf_db"), K(A("select * from t except select 'z', 'w'")), K(PHI()))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:fresh"), A("test:sf_db"))))),
"test:ent_keys holds that an entity table`s keys grouped through cn:entsat (compile:ent_keys_ix, as compile:ent_groups asks it) are the keys the scan of every pair finds (compile:ent_keys_of). Over literal pairs in which the number 1 and the text 1 print alike and are said apart, with another text between them, each text`s keys through the index over <text, <key>> are its keys by the scan over <text, key>: for 1 both, the number first as it is said first; for a its one key; for a text no pair says none. Run first with the indexed keys answered in the wrong order, it failed (ent-keys -> F).",
DEF("test:ent_keys",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_ix"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("1")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), S1(N(1))), S2(A("a"), S1(A("a"))), S2(A("1"), S1(A("1"))), S2(A("b"), S1(A("b"))))))), K(S2(N(1), A("1"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_ix"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("1")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), S1(N(1))), S2(A("a"), S1(A("a"))), S2(A("1"), S1(A("1"))), S2(A("b"), S1(A("b"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_of"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("1")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), N(1)), S2(A("a"), A("a")), S2(A("1"), A("1")), S2(A("b"), A("b")))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_ix"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("a")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), S1(N(1))), S2(A("a"), S1(A("a"))), S2(A("1"), S1(A("1"))), S2(A("b"), S1(A("b"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_of"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("a")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), N(1)), S2(A("a"), A("a")), S2(A("1"), A("1")), S2(A("b"), A("b")))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_ix"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("z")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), S1(N(1))), S2(A("a"), S1(A("a"))), S2(A("1"), S1(A("1"))), S2(A("b"), S1(A("b"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ent_keys_of"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("z")), K(S4(S2(A("1"), N(1)), S2(A("a"), A("a")), S2(A("1"), A("1")), S2(A("b"), A("b"))))))))))),
"test:ent_grow holds that an entity table`s rows read from its column maps are the rows walked key by key (compile:ent_grow, rmap:col_maps, rmap:cm_row against rmap:proj_row). Over the booted store`s Function table, four groups of keys: an operation that is also a transition, a role, an object type, and a group of two keys whose rows are merged, the conceptual data type raw before the object type Function. Each group`s row through the table`s maps is the merge of its keys` rows by rmap:proj_row, and the first row holds more than four values, so neither is empty. Run first with the maps read for the key`s row in the wrong place, it failed (ent-grow -> F).",
DEF("test:eg_groups",
    K(S4(S2(A("apply"), S1(A("apply"))), S2(A("FactTypeHasRole.1"), S1(A("FactTypeHasRole.1"))), S2(A("Function"), S1(A("Function"))), S2(A("raw"), S2(A("raw"), A("Function")))))),
DEF("test:eg_new",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:ent_grow")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:eg_groups"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("Function")), A("id"), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:col_maps"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Function")), A("id")))))))),
DEF("test:eg_old",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S5(A("COMP"), A("rmap:merge_rows"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:proj_row"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("Function")), N(2)))), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:eg_groups"), A("id"))))),
DEF("test:ent_grow",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2))), S3(A("COMP"), A("lt"), S3(A("CONS"), K(N(4)), S5(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("rmap:sp_of"), N(1), N(1))))), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:eg_new"), A("test:eg_old")))),
"test:sync_diff holds that a table the closure moved has only its moved rows deleted and inserted: a scratch table T with a delete trigger, three rows (k1 the closure`s and unchanged, k2 the closure`s and changed, k3 the engine`s alone), the closure`s rows staged in _sync, and sqlite:sync_apply_w_sql run over them. T ends with k1 as it was, k2 as the closure wrote it and k3 untouched, and the trigger saw one delete, k2`s.",
DEF("test:sync_diff",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
