"test:check_onread holds the SQL checks to the in-memory judge over heads computed on read, as test:check_sql holds them over stored fact types: each kind check:all says -- a uniqueness over one role, a mandatory and a subset -- over a head the store computes on read, read where schema:read_place says it is (its view, test:derive_sql). The fixtures are a violating and a clean one of each, made and judged as test:check_sql makes and judges its own: Member has Grade, marked + and given Grade gold by one rule for a Member who is senior and green by another for one who is junior, under Each Member has at most one Grade, so a Member both senior and junior has two; Member belongs to Club, marked * and read off Member joins Club, under Each Member belongs to some Club, which a Member who joins none breaks; and Member is veteran, marked * and read off Member is senior, under If some Member is veteran then that Member is checked, which a senior Member not checked breaks. Member has Nickname gives Member a table, whose key the mandatory reads its instances from. Run first, with check:place reading where a fact type is stored, which no head computed on read is, the SQL checks answered none of the three violations and it failed.",
