"test:delta_write holds the write over a derived fact type read through its view to the answer the gate in memory gives without the cover. The store: Member has Grade, marked +, gold for a senior Member and green for a junior one, under Each Member has at most one Grade, and Club has Motto beside it; m1 senior. The store carrying the cover of its SQL checks (state:sql_cover, as a served store`s boot loads it) is gated in memory without the uniqueness the SQL covers. A fact POST making m1 junior gives m1 two Grades: without the cover it is refused; with it the gate in memory commits it; and the SQL delta of the write refuses it, so the answer the write gives, which re-asks the store without the cover when its program refuses, is the refusal without the cover, byte for byte. A fact POST of Club k1 has Motto red answers with the cover what it answers without, committed, and no check its program asks is one over Member has Grade: the write reads no row of that view. And a second Motto for k1, which Each Club has at most one Motto refuses, is refused with the cover as without it: that uniqueness is its table`s primary key, which a projection of two values for one key never meets, so the cover (delta:boot_cover) leaves it to the gate in memory.",
