"AND A WRITE THAT MOVES THE SCHEMA LEAVES THE PLAN STALE IN THE DATABASE. The cover a boot loads is the plan the last compile stored, and the parts a write asks were planned over that compile`s tables; a write that moves the schema (an applied Domain Change, state:declared moved) lays tables out again, and a boot after it, before a compile, would load the cover and leave to SQL constraints whose parts read the old layout. So that write`s program marks the stored plan`s stamp # in its transaction (delta:write_steps), which no compile reuses and no boot loads a cover from (delta:boot_cover). A store to T when the program of a write from the store with its cover to one whose state:declared moved is that mark alone.",
