    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("AppHasNavigableDomain"), S3(S2(A("tab-app"), A("federation")), S2(A("tab-app"), A("evolution")), S2(A("one-app"), A("evolution")))))))),
"test:app_tabs: an App of several Domains has a tab per Domain, and each tab is its Domain`s root. The fixture is the base store with App tab-app navigating federation and evolution, listed in that order, and App one-app navigating evolution alone. tab-app`s root carries a tabs section, the Domains by name with evolution, the first, selected; it lists Domain Change and not Fetcher, which are evolution`s and federation`s; the address <tab, federation> lists Fetcher and not Domain Change, and its chrome`s Tabs select federation. The detail`s no-selection layer is evolution`s, a tab is the root`s kind on the stack and lands in the master, and one-app has no tabs and lists what tab-app`s home tab lists.",
DEF("test:app_tabs",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_tabs"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app")))), K(S1(S3(A("tabs"), S3(A("evolution"), S2(A("tab"), A("evolution")), A("T")), S3(A("federation"), S2(A("tab"), A("federation")), A("F"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Schema Design")), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Fetcher")), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Fetcher")), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Schema Design")), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:tabs_of"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app"))))), K(S2(S2(A("tab"), S3(S2(A("Title"), A("evolution")), S2(A("NavigationLink"), S2(A("tab"), A("evolution"))), S2(A("Selected"), A("F")))), S2(A("tab"), S3(S2(A("Title"), A("federation")), S2(A("NavigationLink"), S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))), S2(A("Selected"), A("T")))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:vanity_at"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("tab-app"))))), K(A("evolution")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:stackid"), K(S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:prefpane"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("tab"), A("federation"))))), K(A("master")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_tabs"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("one-app"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("one-app")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:root_colls"), S5(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()), K(A("tab-app"))))))), A("test:tb_store")))),
"test:yield_rows: a yield fills the role it names. Over the base store`s Function belongs to Domain, a yield of the second role from the answer is <fact type, subject, value> as it always was; a yield of the first role puts the value first and the subject second; a yield of both roles is the answer`s fact about the entity it names, with no subject in it; and when one of the declared values is missing from the answer, the fact type is not written at all, nor any other fact type of the entity the same path names.",
DEF("test:yield_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("perform:yield_rows"), S4(A("CONS"), K(S3(S4(A("id"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.1"), A("f8")), S4(A("id"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("FunctionHasDescription.1"), A("f8")), S4(A("text"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("FunctionHasDescription.2"), PHI()))), K(A("d8")), A("id")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("perform:yield_rows"), S4(A("CONS"), K(S1(S4(A("p"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.2"), A("d1")))), K(A("f1")), A("id"))), K(S1(S3(A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("f1"), A("d1")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("perform:yield_rows"), S4(A("CONS"), K(S1(S4(A("id"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.1"), A("f9")))), K(A("d9")), A("id"))), K(S1(S3(A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("f9"), A("d9")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("perform:yield_rows"), S4(A("CONS"), K(S2(S4(A("a"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.1"), A("f7")), S4(A("b"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.2"), A("d7")))), K(A("x")), A("id"))), K(S1(S3(A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("f7"), A("d7")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("perform:yield_rows"), S4(A("CONS"), K(S2(S4(A("a"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.1"), A("f7")), S4(A("b"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain.2"), PHI()))), K(A("x")), A("id"))))))),
"test:style_rules: the five style rules an app`s readings leave to a function, decided on texts shaped like the drafts that broke them: a reply opening Hi, on its own line, listing numbered causes and signed Auto.dev Team breaks the sign-off, markup and greeting rules; one opening with a Subject line and Hello, and signed Best, The Auto.dev Team breaks the sign-off, greeting and title rules; a one-paragraph reply merging its greeting breaks none; an em dash breaks the dash rule alone; a short heading between paragraphs breaks the title rule alone. And a decider reads what its constraint spans: spanning a description`s first role it checks every description, and spanning a Function`s domain and a description`s text it checks only the Functions that belong to a domain.",
DEF("test:style_rules",
