"test:ternary_compile: a ternary is read and compiled as one fact type with its three roles in reading order. Employee earns Salary in Year, over Employee, Salary and Year declared, compiles through compile:x to one state:fts row <EmployeeEarnsSalaryInYear, <Employee, Salary, Year>, <<1, 2, 3>>, (), <()>> and one state:readings row whose template places the three players at {0}, {1} and {2} between earns and in, each compared whole. The law runs the lexer: a check that feeds read:parse tokens built by hand and picks fields by position never does.",
DEF("test:tern_x",
    S5(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("e.md"), A("Employee(.id) is an entity type.\nSalary is a value type.\nYear is a value type.\nEmployee earns Salary in Year.\n"), A("tern/e.md")))))),
