"A COMPARISON IN A ROLE PATH IS READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (AREST.tex def:derive, outcomes.md:127). test:rule_cmp reads one readings file: a Violation and three Failures, each occurred at a Timestamp, and five fully derived fact types of a Failure and a Violation, each with one rule whose where compares the two Timestamps: is before (lt), is after (gt), is at least (ge), is at most (le) and equals (an identity). v1 occurred at ts2; f1 at ts3, f2 at ts1, f3 at ts2. For each head, the rows lambda`s read over the cells answers (derive:on_read) and the rows its view answers in the database the compile lays out (test:dq_sql, as test:derive_sql reads them) are the expected ones: succeeds f1, precedes f2, trails f1 and f3, leads f2 and f3, matches f3, each with v1. Run first, before rpath read a where outside a negation, every head read no rule, and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:rc_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("cmp.md"), A("Violation(.id) is an entity type.\nFailure(.id) is an entity type.\nTimestamp is a value type.\nViolation occurred at Timestamp.\n  Each Violation occurred at at most one Timestamp.\nFailure occurred at Timestamp.\n  Each Failure occurred at at most one Timestamp.\nFailure succeeds Violation. *\n  Each Failure, Violation combination occurs at most once in the population of Failure succeeds Violation.\n* Failure succeeds Violation iff that Violation occurred at some Timestamp1 and that Failure occurred at some Timestamp2 where Timestamp1 is before Timestamp2.\nFailure precedes Violation. *\n  Each Failure, Violation combination occurs at most once in the population of Failure precedes Violation.\n* Failure precedes Violation iff that Violation occurred at some Timestamp1 and that Failure occurred at some Timestamp2 where Timestamp1 is after Timestamp2.\nFailure trails Violation. *\n  Each Failure, Violation combination occurs at most once in the population of Failure trails Violation.\n* Failure trails Violation iff that Violation occurred at some Timestamp1 and that Failure occurred at some Timestamp2 where Timestamp2 is at least Timestamp1.\nFailure leads Violation. *\n  Each Failure, Violation combination occurs at most once in the population of Failure leads Violation.\n* Failure leads Violation iff that Violation occurred at some Timestamp1 and that Failure occurred at some Timestamp2 where Timestamp2 is at most Timestamp1.\nFailure matches Violation. *\n  Each Failure, Violation combination occurs at most once in the population of Failure matches Violation.\n* Failure matches Violation iff that Violation occurred at some Timestamp1 and that Failure occurred at some Timestamp2 where Timestamp1 equals Timestamp2.\nViolation 'v1' occurred at Timestamp 'ts2'.\nFailure 'f1' occurred at Timestamp 'ts3'.\nFailure 'f2' occurred at Timestamp 'ts1'.\nFailure 'f3' occurred at Timestamp 'ts2'.\n"), A("cmp/cmp.md"))))),
DEF("test:rc_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rc_files"))),
DEF("test:rc_want",
    K(S5(S2(A("FailureSucceedsViolation"), S1(S2(A("f1"), A("v1")))), S2(A("FailurePrecedesViolation"), S1(S2(A("f2"), A("v1")))), S2(A("FailureTrailsViolation"), S2(S2(A("f1"), A("v1")), S2(A("f3"), A("v1")))), S2(A("FailureLeadsViolation"), S2(S2(A("f2"), A("v1")), S2(A("f3"), A("v1")))), S2(A("FailureMatchesViolation"), S1(S2(A("f3"), A("v1"))))))),
"<<derived fact type, rows>, <database, env, store>> to T when lambda`s read over the store and the database both answer the rows.",
DEF("test:rc_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:dq_sql"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1))))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict over the five heads, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:rc_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rc_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rc_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:rc_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_cmp",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:rc_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-cmp.db")))))),
"SOME OTHER AND THAT ROLEINSTANCE ARE READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (AREST.tex def:derive; core.md:1585). test:rule_other reads one readings file declaring Fact fills Role, objectified as RoleInstance, which uses an Object Type Instance, and Role is used in Reading, objectified as RoleIsUsedInReading, which has a Position, with the metamodel`s own rule: Fact1 joins Fact2 iff Fact1 fills some Role1 and that RoleInstance uses some Object Type Instance and that Role1 is used in some Reading1 and that RoleIsUsedInReading has Position 2 and some other Fact2 fills some Role2 and that RoleInstance uses that Object Type Instance and that Role2 is used in some Reading2 and that RoleIsUsedInReading has Position 1. fa fills ra1 and ra2, fb fills rb1 and rb2; fa.ra1 uses va, fa.ra2 vb, fb.rb1 vb, fb.rb2 vc; ra1 and ra2 are used in rda, rb1 and rb2 in rdb, at Positions 1 and 2. So fa`s position-2 role uses vb, which fb`s position-1 role uses: fa joins fb, and nothing else does, fb with itself least of all. lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and the view in the database the compile lays out (test:dq_sql) both answer exactly <fa, fb>. Run first, before rpath read other, an objectification reference or a numeral, the rule read # and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:ro_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("other.md"), A("Fact(.id) is an entity type.\nRole(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance(.id) is an entity type.\nReading(.id) is an entity type.\nPosition is a value type.\nFunction(.id) is an entity type.\nFact fills Role.\n  Each Fact, Role combination occurs at most once in the population of Fact fills Role.\nRoleInstance objectifies \"Fact fills Role\".\nRoleInstance is a subtype of Function.\nRoleInstance uses Object Type Instance.\n  Each RoleInstance uses at most one Object Type Instance.\nRole is used in Reading.\n  Each Role, Reading combination occurs at most once in the population of Role is used in Reading.\nRoleIsUsedInReading objectifies \"Role is used in Reading\".\nRoleIsUsedInReading is a subtype of Function.\nRoleIsUsedInReading has Position.\n  Each RoleIsUsedInReading has at most one Position.\nFact joins Fact. *\n  Each Fact, Fact combination occurs at most once in the population of Fact joins Fact.\n* Fact1 joins Fact2 iff Fact1 fills some Role1 and that RoleInstance uses some Object Type Instance and that Role1 is used in some Reading1 and that RoleIsUsedInReading has Position 2 and some other Fact2 fills some Role2 and that RoleInstance uses that Object Type Instance and that Role2 is used in some Reading2 and that RoleIsUsedInReading has Position 1.\nFact 'fa' fills Role 'ra1'.\nFact 'fa' fills Role 'ra2'.\nFact 'fb' fills Role 'rb1'.\nFact 'fb' fills Role 'rb2'.\nRoleInstance 'fa.ra1' uses Object Type Instance 'va'.\nRoleInstance 'fa.ra2' uses Object Type Instance 'vb'.\nRoleInstance 'fb.rb1' uses Object Type Instance 'vb'.\nRoleInstance 'fb.rb2' uses Object Type Instance 'vc'.\nRole 'ra1' is used in Reading 'rda'.\nRole 'ra2' is used in Reading 'rda'.\nRole 'rb1' is used in Reading 'rdb'.\nRole 'rb2' is used in Reading 'rdb'.\nRoleIsUsedInReading 'ra1.rda' has Position 1.\nRoleIsUsedInReading 'ra2.rda' has Position 2.\nRoleIsUsedInReading 'rb1.rdb' has Position 1.\nRoleIsUsedInReading 'rb2.rdb' has Position 2.\n"), A("other/other.md"))))),
DEF("test:ro_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ro_files"))),
DEF("test:ro_want",
    K(S1(S2(A("FactJoinsFact"), S1(S2(A("fa"), A("fb"))))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict over Fact joins Fact, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:ro_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rc_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ro_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:ro_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_other",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:ro_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:ro_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-other.db")))))),
"A CALCULATED VALUE AND AN AGGREGATE IN A ROLE PATH ARE READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (AREST.tex def:derive: a derived role bound to an admitted deterministic total function of bound values, or to an aggregate reducing a finite bag to one scalar). test:rule_calc reads one readings file: t1 has Positions p1, p2, p3 with Amounts 5, 7, 5, t2 has p4 with 2; t1 has Base 10 and Step 3, t2 4 and 4. Four fully derived fact types: Task has Count, the count of its Positions (t1 3, t2 1); Task has Total, the sum of its Positions` Amounts (t1 17, the two 5s each counted, t2 2); Task has Next, Base plus Step (t1 13, t2 8); Task has Gap, Base minus Step (t1 7, t2 0). lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and the view in the database (test:dq_sql) both answer them. Run first, before rpath read either, every head read no rule and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:ra_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("calc.md"), A("Task(.id) is an entity type.\nPosition(.id) is an entity type.\nAmount is a value type.\nCount is a value type.\nTotal is a value type.\nBase is a value type.\nStep is a value type.\nNext is a value type.\nGap is a value type.\nTask has Position.\n  Each Task, Position combination occurs at most once in the population of Task has Position.\nPosition has Amount.\n  Each Position has at most one Amount.\nTask has Base.\n  Each Task has at most one Base.\nTask has Step.\n  Each Task has at most one Step.\nTask has Count. *\n  Each Task has at most one Count.\n* Task1 has Count iff Count is the count of Position1 where Task1 has Position1.\nTask has Total. *\n  Each Task has at most one Total.\n* Task1 has Total iff Total is the sum of Amount1 where Task1 has Position1 and Position1 has Amount1.\nTask has Next. *\n  Each Task has at most one Next.\n* Task1 has Next iff Task1 has Base and Task1 has Step and Base plus Step is Next.\nTask has Gap. *\n  Each Task has at most one Gap.\n* Task1 has Gap iff Task1 has Base and Task1 has Step and Gap is Base minus Step.\nTask 't1' has Position 'p1'.\nTask 't1' has Position 'p2'.\nTask 't1' has Position 'p3'.\nTask 't2' has Position 'p4'.\nPosition 'p1' has Amount '5'.\nPosition 'p2' has Amount '7'.\nPosition 'p3' has Amount '5'.\nPosition 'p4' has Amount '2'.\nTask 't1' has Base '10'.\nTask 't1' has Step '3'.\nTask 't2' has Base '4'.\nTask 't2' has Step '4'.\n"), A("calc/calc.md"))))),
DEF("test:ra_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ra_files"))),
DEF("test:ra_want",
    K(S4(S2(A("TaskHasCount"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("3")), S2(A("t2"), A("1")))), S2(A("TaskHasTotal"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("17")), S2(A("t2"), A("2")))), S2(A("TaskHasNext"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("13")), S2(A("t2"), A("8")))), S2(A("TaskHasGap"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("7")), S2(A("t2"), A("0"))))))),
"<<derived fact type, rows>, <database, env, store>> to T when lambda`s read over the store and the database both answer the rows, each value said as text (value:text, an integer then as its digits): a count is a number in memory and its text in a database`s row.",
DEF("test:ra_text",
    S2(A("ALPHA"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("system:isnum"), A("ntoa"), A("id")), A("value:text"))))),
DEF("test:ra_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("test:ra_text"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("test:ra_text"), A("test:dq_sql"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1))))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict over the four heads, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:ra_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ra_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ra_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:ra_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_calc",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:ra_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:ra_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-calc.db")))))),
"A RECURSIVE RULE AND A DISJUNCTIVE BODY ARE READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE, AND A VALUE-INTRODUCING CYCLE IS REFUSED (AREST.tex def:derive, the union of a derived fact type`s rules; lem:finite, recursion admitted where no value-introducing rule lies on a cycle and negation is stratified). test:rule_rec reads one readings file with every recursive shape the corpora use (over the base and the app corpora): a transitive closure reading its head twice (core.md`s Domain reaches Domain, Domain draws on Domain, state.md`s Status reaches Status in State Machine Definition, here with its third role held fixed), a right-linear one (Derivation Rule reaches Derivation Rule), one whose step is an if-then (imports.md`s JS Package reaches JS Package), a nesting that reads its head twice through another fact type (Status is defined in State Machine Definition, Transition exits Status in State Machine Definition, the second with two such rules), a linear one beside a negation (Status is leaf initial in State Machine Definition) and a symmetric if-then (Element transforms by changing one quality to Element); and the disjunctive bodies: a base and a step in one rule (Layer depends on Layer), an or of two clauses, and an or of two arms each with its negation (Element transforms`s own rule). Each derives what its rules say over a chain a, b, c, d, a nesting of three boxes and a second box beside it, in lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and in the views (test:dq_sql). Node has Level, which reads itself under a sum of two values, is no head rpath reads and is said as a value_cycle; Node pairs with Node, an if-then over an asserted fact type, is a constraint and no rule. Run first over the lambda before it, the three disjunctive heads read nothing in memory or in the views, Node has Level read to # unsaid (its read of itself coming after the calculation that needs it), and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:rr_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("rec.md"), A("Node(.id) is an entity type.\nBox(.id) is an entity type.\nItem(.id) is an entity type.\nLevel is a value type.\nStep is a value type.\nNode links to Node.\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node links to Node.\nNode serves Node.\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node serves Node.\nNode guards Node.\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node guards Node.\nNode steps to Node in Box.\n  Each Node, Node, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Node steps to Node in Box.\nItem is in Box.\n  Each Item, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Item is in Box.\nItem is first in Box.\n  Each Item, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Item is first in Box.\nNode pairs with Node.\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node pairs with Node.\nItem opens Box.\n  Each Item has at most one Box.\nNode is from Item.\n  Each Node has at most one Item.\nNode has Step.\n  Each Node has at most one Step.\nIf Node1 pairs with Node2, then Node2 pairs with Node1.\nNode reaches Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node reaches Node.\n* Node1 reaches Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2.\n* Node1 reaches Node3 iff Node1 reaches Node2 and Node2 reaches Node3.\nNode chains to Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node chains to Node.\n* Node1 chains to Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2.\n* Node1 chains to Node3 iff Node1 links to Node2 and Node2 chains to Node3.\nNode goes to Node in Box. *\n  Each Node, Node, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Node goes to Node in Box.\n* Node1 goes to Node2 in Box iff Node1 steps to Node2 in Box.\n* Node1 goes to Node3 in Box iff Node1 goes to Node2 in that Box and Node2 goes to Node3 in that Box.\nItem is held in Box. *\n  Each Item, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Item is held in Box.\n* Item is held in Box iff that Item is in that Box.\n* Item1 is held in Box1 iff that Item1 is held in some Box2 and some Item2 opens that Box2 and that Item2 is held in that Box1.\nNode leaves Item in Box. *\n  Each Node, Item, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Node leaves Item in Box.\n* Node leaves Item in Box iff that Node is from that Item and that Item is in that Box.\n* Node leaves Item1 in Box1 iff that Node leaves that Item1 in some Box2 and some Item2 opens that Box2 and that Item2 is held in that Box1.\n* Node leaves Item1 in Box1 iff that Item1 is held in some Box2 and some Item2 opens that Box2 and that Node leaves that Item2 in that Box1.\nItem is leaf first in Box. *\n  Each Item, Box combination occurs at most once in the population of Item is leaf first in Box.\n* Item is leaf first in Box1 iff that Item is first in that Box1 and it is not true that that Item opens some Box2.\n* Item1 is leaf first in Box1 iff some Item2 is first in that Box1 and that Item2 opens some Box2 and that Item1 is leaf first in that Box2.\nNode mirrors Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node mirrors Node.\n* Node1 mirrors Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2.\nIf some Node1 mirrors some Node2 then that Node2 mirrors that Node1.\nNode joins Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node joins Node.\n* Node1 joins Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2.\nIf Node1 joins Node2 and Node2 joins Node3 then Node1 joins Node3.\nNode depends on Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node depends on Node.\n* Node1 depends on Node2 iff Node2 serves Node1 or Node1 depends on some Node3 and that Node3 depends on Node2.\nNode backs Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node backs Node.\n* Node1 backs Node2 iff Node2 serves Node1 or Node1 links to Node2.\nNode swaps with Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node swaps with Node.\n* Node1 swaps with Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2 and it is not true that Node2 guards Node1 or Node2 guards Node1 and it is not true that Node1 links to Node2.\nIf some Node1 swaps with some Node2 then that Node2 swaps with that Node1.\nNode has Level. *\n  Each Node, Level combination occurs at most once in the population of Node has Level.\n* Node has Level iff that Node has Step and Step plus Step is Level.\n* Node1 has Level2 iff Node1 links to Node2 and Node2 has Level1 and Node1 has Step and Level1 plus Step is Level2.\nNode 'a' links to Node 'b'.\nNode 'b' links to Node 'c'.\nNode 'c' links to Node 'd'.\nNode 'a' serves Node 'b'.\nNode 'b' serves Node 'c'.\nNode 'c' serves Node 'd'.\nNode 'a' guards Node 'b'.\nNode 'a' pairs with Node 'b'.\nNode 'a' steps to Node 'b' in Box 'X'.\nNode 'b' steps to Node 'c' in Box 'X'.\nNode 'c' steps to Node 'd' in Box 'X'.\nNode 'a' steps to Node 'b' in Box 'Y'.\nItem 'i1' is in Box 'B1'.\nItem 'i1' opens Box 'B2'.\nItem 'i2' is in Box 'B2'.\nItem 'i2' opens Box 'B3'.\nItem 'i3' is in Box 'B3'.\nItem 'i1' is first in Box 'B1'.\nItem 'i2' is first in Box 'B2'.\nItem 'i3' is first in Box 'B3'.\nNode 'a' is from Item 'i1'.\nNode 'b' is from Item 'i3'.\nNode 'a' has Step '1'.\nNode 'b' has Step '1'.\n"), A("rec/rec.md"))))),
DEF("test:rr_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rr_files"))),
DEF("test:rr_want",
    K(S(S2(A("NodeReachesNode"), S(S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("c")), S2(A("b"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("d")))), S2(A("NodeChainsToNode"), S(S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("c")), S2(A("b"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("d")))), S2(A("NodeJoinsNode"), S(S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("c")), S2(A("b"), A("d")), S2(A("a"), A("d")))), S2(A("NodeGoesToNodeInBox"), S(S3(A("a"), A("b"), A("X")), S3(A("b"), A("c"), A("X")), S3(A("c"), A("d"), A("X")), S3(A("a"), A("b"), A("Y")), S3(A("a"), A("c"), A("X")), S3(A("b"), A("d"), A("X")), S3(A("a"), A("d"), A("X")))), S2(A("ItemIsHeldInBox"), S(S2(A("i1"), A("B1")), S2(A("i2"), A("B2")), S2(A("i3"), A("B3")), S2(A("i2"), A("B1")), S2(A("i3"), A("B2")), S2(A("i3"), A("B1")))), S2(A("NodeLeavesItemInBox"), S(S3(A("a"), A("i1"), A("B1")), S3(A("b"), A("i3"), A("B3")), S3(A("b"), A("i3"), A("B2")), S3(A("b"), A("i3"), A("B1")), S3(A("a"), A("i2"), A("B1")), S3(A("a"), A("i3"), A("B1")))), S2(A("ItemIsLeafFirstInBox"), S(S2(A("i3"), A("B3")), S2(A("i3"), A("B2")), S2(A("i3"), A("B1")))), S2(A("NodeMirrorsNode"), S(S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")), S2(A("b"), A("a")), S2(A("c"), A("b")), S2(A("d"), A("c")))), S2(A("NodeDependsOnNode"), S(S2(A("b"), A("a")), S2(A("c"), A("b")), S2(A("d"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("a")), S2(A("d"), A("b")), S2(A("d"), A("a")))), S2(A("NodeBacksNode"), S(S2(A("b"), A("a")), S2(A("c"), A("b")), S2(A("d"), A("c")), S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")))), S2(A("NodeSwapsWithNode"), S(S2(A("a"), A("b")), S2(A("b"), A("c")), S2(A("c"), A("d")), S2(A("b"), A("a")), S2(A("c"), A("b")), S2(A("d"), A("c"))))))),
"<<derived fact type, rows>, <database, env, store>> to T when lambda`s read over the store and the database both answer the rows.",
DEF("test:rr_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(2)))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:dq_sql"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1))))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict over the heads, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:rr_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rr_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rr_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:rr_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
"T when Node has Level and Node pairs with Node are no heads rpath reads, and the reader says Node has Level`s value cycle, and only it.",
DEF("test:rr_refused",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("NodeHasLevel")), A("test:rr_heads"))),
