DEF("test:rule_rec",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rr_refused"),
       S6(A("COMP"), A("test:rr_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:rr_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-rec.db")))))))),
"THE RULES THAT RUN ARE ADMITTED, AND A STORE WHOSE COMPILE REFUSED ONE IS NOT (AREST.tex lem:finite, cor:finitecheck). test:admission holds that the store under test admits its rules (derive:admitted) and that it has some (rpath:running: the base`s 71, over its 44 heads), and that test:rule_rec`s store, whose Node has Level reads itself under a sum, is not admitted and keeps that head, and only it, as refused (state:refused). Run first, before derive:admitted read the rules that run, admission was derive:stratified over derive:all_rules, which answers no rule, and the law did not answer T.",
DEF("test:admission",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       A("derive:admitted"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("rpath:running")),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("derive:admitted"), A("test:rr_store")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("rpath:refused_of"), A("test:rr_store")), K(S1(A("NodeHasLevel")))))))),
DEF("test:rr_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:rr_cells"))),
"test:branch_neg: a negation over legs that share the variable it introduces is one anti-join, through the reader, the derivation and the SQL checks as test:delta_law holds them. Member is free iff that Member is listed and it is not true that some Booking holds that Member and that Booking is confirmed, and a free Member must be checked. m1, listed, with one Booking b1 that is confirmed, is not free; b1 losing its confirmation frees m1 unchecked (V); m1 gaining a second, unconfirmed Booking beside b1 leaves it not free (C). The reader ended the negation at the next and: it read `that Booking is confirmed` as a positive leg nothing binds, and declined the rule, so V answered F.",
DEF("test:bn_fx",
    K(S2(S6(A("Name is a value type.\nMember(.Name) is an entity type.\nBooking(.Name) is an entity type.\nMember is listed.\nMember is checked.\nBooking holds Member.\n  Each Booking holds at most one Member.\nBooking is confirmed.\nMember is free. *\n* Member is free iff that Member is listed and it is not true that some Booking holds that Member and that Booking is confirmed.\nIf some Member is free then that Member is checked.\n"), S3(S2(A("MemberIsListed"), S1(S1(A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingHoldsMember"), S1(S2(A("b1"), A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingIsConfirmed"), S1(S1(A("b1"))))), S2(S2(A("m1"), A("Member")), S2(A("b1"), A("Booking"))), S2(S2(A("MemberIsListed"), S1(S1(A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingHoldsMember"), S1(S2(A("b1"), A("m1"))))), S2(S2(A("m1"), A("Member")), S2(A("b1"), A("Booking"))), A("V")), S6(A("Name is a value type.\nMember(.Name) is an entity type.\nBooking(.Name) is an entity type.\nMember is listed.\nMember is checked.\nBooking holds Member.\n  Each Booking holds at most one Member.\nBooking is confirmed.\nMember is free. *\n* Member is free iff that Member is listed and it is not true that some Booking holds that Member and that Booking is confirmed.\nIf some Member is free then that Member is checked.\n"), S3(S2(A("MemberIsListed"), S1(S1(A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingHoldsMember"), S1(S2(A("b1"), A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingIsConfirmed"), S1(S1(A("b1"))))), S2(S2(A("m1"), A("Member")), S2(A("b1"), A("Booking"))), S3(S2(A("MemberIsListed"), S1(S1(A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingHoldsMember"), S2(S2(A("b1"), A("m1")), S2(A("b2"), A("m1")))), S2(A("BookingIsConfirmed"), S1(S1(A("b1"))))), S3(S2(A("m1"), A("Member")), S2(A("b1"), A("Booking")), S2(A("b2"), A("Booking"))), A("C"))))),
DEF("test:branch_neg",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:dl_one")), A("test:bn_fx"))),
"test:flip_declared holds compile:ip_why_flipped to the fact types the new store declares: when the only fact type whose readings` facts read back none is GoneHasURL, which the new store does not declare, there is no refusal; with KeptHasURL, which it declares, beside it there is.",
