    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ip_why_flipped"), K(S3(PHI(), S1(S2(A("GoneHasURL"), S2(A("g1"), A("u")))), S1(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S1(S5(A("KeptHasURL"), S2(A("Kept"), A("URL")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()))))))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ip_why_flipped"), K(S3(PHI(), S2(S2(A("GoneHasURL"), S2(A("g1"), A("u"))), S2(A("KeptHasURL"), S2(A("k1"), A("u")))), S1(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S1(S5(A("KeptHasURL"), S2(A("Kept"), A("URL")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI())))))))))))),
"test:taken_put holds main:cf_w2, the put of a retract or a replace over a store served from its database, to what it records. <store, fact type F, the rows put, the population held, the rows the cells hold> over a store that has already taken <a, 1> of F: putting <b, 2> where the population held is <b, 2> and <c, 3> and the cells hold none takes <c, 3> beside <a, 1> and keeps nothing in the cell, <b, 2> being the database`s already; putting <a, 1> and <d, 4> where the population held is <b, 2> and <d, 4> and the cells hold <d, 4> takes <b, 2> alone, <a, 1> being put again, and keeps both rows put. Before it the retract and the replace started from the cells alone, and over a store booted from its database a DELETE committed nothing and a PUT was refused.",
