"test:fn_cache holds the map and the in-place compile to the design: a ** fact type a Function yields is the Function`s cache, and a fully derived fact type no rule derives and no Function yields reads empty. Over test:ry_fx, LawRyYld, which law-ry-fn yields, is among compile:ip_cached and not compile:ip_ruleless, and LawRyFed, federated at a JSON Path and yielded by no Function, is among compile:ip_ruleless; compile:ip_excluded leaves out neither, so the in-place compile keeps LawRyYld`s facts and drops LawRyFed`s by name (compile:ip_rt_split). rmap:gate lets a fully derived map input through when it is among the caches, so the Function`s cache keeps its table, and stops it otherwise. Run without compile:ip_cached, it failed.",
