"test:put_sp holds sqlite:put_sp to the full rows its sparse rows stand for. A table of four columns, made with no default, is given the columns of positions 1, 3 and 4, position 2 being held by no column, as the stage is given a table`s columns without the engine`s; four sparse rows are put: one holding positions 1 and 3; one holding 4, 2 and 1 in that order; one holding none; one holding 5, past every column, and 3. Read back in rowid order they are the four rows, each column a row does not hold NULL (#), the pairs whose position no column holds put nowhere. Run first with the rows put in reverse order, it failed (put-sp -> F): sqlite:sync_apply_sql inserts from the stage in rowid order, so the order is part of what put_sp promises.",
