"test:desc_named holds derive:desc_named to the descriptor store:fts holds of the name. A store of one cell, state:fts, and no state:fts_boot, so store:fts_cached is F and both are found among the descriptors as state:fts holds them: AHasB`s rows are held nested, <<a b> <c d>> and <<e f>>, as appended rows are, and CHasD`s are flat. derive:desc_named of each name is theta:find_desc of it in store:fts, AHasB`s with its three rows unfolded, and of a name no descriptor has it is <> as theta:find_desc`s is. Run with derive:desc_named finding without unfolding the descriptor found, it failed.",
