"THE KERNEL`S CONSTRAINT OBJECTS, over a literal store: Person has Name with a uniqueness on its first role, an external uniqueness across Person has Name and Person likes Person, and an irreflexive ring on Person likes Person, its span positions given once as text and once as numbers, as the carriers and the tables hand them. The external uniqueness`s sequence is in Position order; V is the two rows giving p1 two names, each naming its constraint; the external uniqueness and the ring, which no family takes yet, are listed as unbuilt. It failed first with uniqueness applied at the wrong positions.",
DEF("test:kc_store", K(S9(S3(A("CELL"), A("FactTypeHasRole"), S4(S2(A("PersonHasName"), A("PersonHasName.1")), S2(A("PersonHasName"), A("PersonHasName.2")), S2(A("PersonLikesPerson"), A("PersonLikesPerson.1")), S2(A("PersonLikesPerson"), A("PersonLikesPerson.2")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType"), S3(S2(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1"), A("UC")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1"), A("UC")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson"), A("IR")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ConstraintHasModalityOfModalityType"), S3(S2(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1"), A("Alethic")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1"), A("Alethic")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson"), A("Deontic")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ConstraintSpan"), S5(S2(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1"), A("PersonHasName.1")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1"), A("PersonLikesPerson.1")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1"), A("PersonHasName.2")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson"), A("PersonLikesPerson.1")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson"), A("PersonLikesPerson.2")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ConstraintSpanHasSequenceNumber"), S5(S2(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1.PersonHasName.1"), A("1")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1.PersonLikesPerson.1"), N(1)), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1.PersonHasName.2"), N(1)), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson.PersonLikesPerson.1"), A("1")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson.PersonLikesPerson.2"), A("1")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ConstraintSpanHasPosition"), S5(S2(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1.PersonHasName.1"), A("1")), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1.PersonLikesPerson.1"), N(2)), S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1.PersonHasName.2"), N(1)), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson.PersonLikesPerson.1"), A("1")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson.PersonLikesPerson.2"), A("2")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonHasName"), S3(S2(A("p1"), A("Ann")), S2(A("p1"), A("Bea")), S2(A("p2"), A("Cy")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonLikesPerson"), S1(S2(A("p1"), A("p2")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), PHI())))),
DEF("test:kernel_constraints", S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("kernel:seq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), A("id"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("kernel:constraints"), A("test:kc_store"))))), K(N(1)))), K(S2(S2(A("PersonHasName"), N(2)), S2(A("PersonLikesPerson"), N(1)))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("kernel:violations"), A("test:kc_store")), K(S2(S3(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1"), A("Alethic"), S2(A("p1"), A("Ann"))), S3(A("UC:in:PersonHasName#1"), A("Alethic"), S2(A("p1"), A("Bea"))))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("kernel:unbuilt"), A("test:kc_store")), K(S2(S2(A("UC:en:PersonHasName#2+PersonLikesPerson#1"), A("UC")), S2(A("IR:PersonLikesPerson"), A("IR"))))))))),
"AN AGGREGATE WHOSE REST DOES NOT READ IS UNREAD AND SAID (AREST.tex prop:spec and def:fragment: a rule is admitted only as a role path over declared fact types). test:agg_unread reads one readings file twice: Task has Position, Task has Count fully derived, and the rule Task1 has Count iff Count is the count of Position1 where Task1 has Position1, then the same rule with a second clause no reading declares, and Position1 is frobbed. The first reads to its count of Task has Position projected on the Task; the second reads to no head (read:state_rpaths) and is said by its one clause that names no reading, Position1 is frobbed, unresolved (read:rule_check_rows), and not by the aggregate clause, which reads. Run first, before rpath:aggitems2 took a rest of [#] for one that does not read, the read threw selector 1 on atom # (rpath:isnegi, from rpath:aggrecipe), and before the aggregate clause was read by its rest, the aggregate clause was said unresolved beside it.",
DEF("test:au_ok_text",
    K(S2(A("agg.md"), A("Task(.id) is an entity type.\nPosition(.id) is an entity type.\nCount is a value type.\nTask has Position.\n  Each Task, Position combination occurs at most once in the population of Task has Position.\nTask has Count. *\n  Each Task has at most one Count.\n* Task1 has Count iff Count is the count of Position1 where Task1 has Position1.\n")))),
DEF("test:au_bad_text",
    K(S2(A("agg.md"), A("Task(.id) is an entity type.\nPosition(.id) is an entity type.\nCount is a value type.\nTask has Position.\n  Each Task, Position combination occurs at most once in the population of Task has Position.\nTask has Count. *\n  Each Task has at most one Count.\n* Task1 has Count iff Count is the count of Position1 where Task1 has Position1 and Position1 is frobbed.\n")))),
DEF("test:au_x",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("read:x_full"), A("read:x_of"), A("compile:text_rows"))),
DEF("test:agg_unread",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("read:state_rpaths"), A("test:au_x"), A("test:au_ok_text")),
          K(S1(S2(A("TaskHasCount"), S1(S3(A("proj"), S3(A("count"), S3(A("proj"), A("TaskHasPosition"), S2(N(1), N(2))), N(1)), S2(N(1), N(2))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("read:state_rpaths"), A("test:au_x"), A("test:au_bad_text")), K(PHI()))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S5(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3))), A("read:rule_check_rows"), A("test:au_x"), A("test:au_bad_text")),
          K(S1(S3(A("unresolved"), A("Position1 is frobbed"), A("reported"))))))))),
"A UNIVERSAL IS A NEGATED EXISTENTIAL WITH A NESTED NEGATION, AND IT IS READ IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (Halpin: each Line Item of that Order is shipped, said as no Line Item of that Order is not shipped; AREST.tex def:derive, and lem:finite, negation stratified). test:rule_univ reads one readings file: Line Item is of Order, Line Item is shipped, Customer has Order, and two fully derived unaries, Order is fully shipped iff that Order is placed and no Line Item of that Order is not shipped, and Customer is fully served iff that Customer is active and no Order of that Customer is not fully shipped, the second over the first, so the inner negation of the second reads a head that is itself a negation, a stratum below. Order of that Customer is read through Customer has Order, of as the inverse of has. o1 has l1 and l2, both shipped; o2 has l3, shipped, and l4, not; o3 has none. c1 has o1 and o3, c2 has o1 and o2, c3 has none. So o1 and o3 are fully shipped, o3 vacuously, and c1 and c3 are fully served, c3 vacuously; lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and the views in the database the compile lays out (test:dq_sql) both answer exactly those. Run first, before a negation`s body was read as items, both rules read to # and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:ru_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("univ.md"), A("Order(.id) is an entity type.\nLine Item(.id) is an entity type.\nCustomer(.id) is an entity type.\nLine Item is of Order.\n  Each Line Item is of at most one Order.\nLine Item is shipped.\nOrder is placed.\nCustomer has Order.\n  Each Customer, Order combination occurs at most once in the population of Customer has Order.\nCustomer is active.\nOrder is fully shipped. *\n* Order is fully shipped iff that Order is placed and no Line Item of that Order is not shipped.\nCustomer is fully served. *\n* Customer is fully served iff that Customer is active and no Order of that Customer is not fully shipped.\nOrder 'o1' is placed.\nOrder 'o2' is placed.\nOrder 'o3' is placed.\nLine Item 'l1' is of Order 'o1'.\nLine Item 'l2' is of Order 'o1'.\nLine Item 'l3' is of Order 'o2'.\nLine Item 'l4' is of Order 'o2'.\nLine Item 'l1' is shipped.\nLine Item 'l2' is shipped.\nLine Item 'l3' is shipped.\nCustomer 'c1' is active.\nCustomer 'c2' is active.\nCustomer 'c3' is active.\nCustomer 'c1' has Order 'o1'.\nCustomer 'c1' has Order 'o3'.\nCustomer 'c2' has Order 'o1'.\nCustomer 'c2' has Order 'o2'.\n"), A("univ/univ.md"))))),
DEF("test:ru_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ru_files"))),
DEF("test:ru_want",
    K(S2(S2(A("OrderIsFullyShipped"), S2(S1(A("o1")), S1(A("o3")))), S2(A("CustomerIsFullyServed"), S2(S1(A("c1")), S1(A("c3"))))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict over the two heads, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:ru_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rc_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ru_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:ru_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_univ",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:ru_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:ru_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-univ.db")))))),
"A COMPARISON WITH A QUOTED VALUE IS READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (AREST.tex def:derive, a value quoted in the rule). test:rule_cmplit reads one readings file: Log Entry has HTTP Status, and two fully derived unaries whose where compares the HTTP Status with a value the rule quotes, Log Entry is an error iff that Log Entry has some HTTP Status where that HTTP Status is at least 400 (a numeral), and Log Entry is a success iff ... is less than `300` (a quoted value). e1 has 200, e2 404, e3 500, e4 302: e2 and e3 are errors and e1 a success, in lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and in the views (test:dq_sql). Run first, before rpath read a quoted side, both rules read to # and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:rl_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("lit.md"), A("Log Entry(.id) is an entity type.\nHTTP Status is a value type.\nLog Entry has HTTP Status.\n  Each Log Entry has at most one HTTP Status.\nLog Entry is an error. *\n* Log Entry is an error iff that Log Entry has some HTTP Status where that HTTP Status is at least 400.\nLog Entry is a success. *\n* Log Entry is a success iff that Log Entry has some HTTP Status where that HTTP Status is less than '300'.\nLog Entry 'e1' has HTTP Status '200'.\nLog Entry 'e2' has HTTP Status '404'.\nLog Entry 'e3' has HTTP Status '500'.\nLog Entry 'e4' has HTTP Status '302'.\n"), A("lit/lit.md"))))),
DEF("test:rl_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rl_files"))),
DEF("test:rl_want",
    K(S2(S2(A("LogEntryIsAnError"), S2(S1(A("e2")), S1(A("e3")))), S2(A("LogEntryIsASuccess"), S1(S1(A("e1"))))))),
DEF("test:rl_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rc_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rl_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:rl_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_cmplit",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:rl_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:rl_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-cmplit.db")))))),
"A UNIVERSAL WITH NO POSITIVE LEG DERIVES OVER A SUPERTYPE WHOSE INSTANCES ARE ALL AT ITS SUBTYPES (instances.md:169-173; Halpin: subtyping is population inclusion). test:rule_ext reads one readings file declaring Party with Person and Company its subtypes, Party places Order, the classification Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type with p1 a Person and c1 and c2 Companies, and Party is dormant iff it is not true that that Party places some Order, whose body opens with its negation. Its extent is every Party, and no instance is classified at Party, so it is the classification at Party, at Person and at Company; c1 places o1, so p1 and c2 are dormant, in lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and in the views (test:dq_sql). Run first, before an extent held its subtypes` instances, the extent was empty and the law answered F.",
DEF("test:re_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("ext.md"), A("Party(.id) is an entity type.\nPerson is a subtype of Party.\nCompany is a subtype of Party.\nOrder(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\n  Each Object Type Instance, Object Type combination occurs at most once in the population of Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nParty places Order.\n  Each Order is placed by at most one Party.\nParty is dormant. *\n* Party is dormant iff it is not true that that Party places some Order.\nObject Type Instance 'p1' is instance of Object Type 'Person'.\nObject Type Instance 'c1' is instance of Object Type 'Company'.\nObject Type Instance 'c2' is instance of Object Type 'Company'.\nParty 'c1' places Order 'o1'.\n"), A("ext/ext.md"))))),
DEF("test:re_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:re_files"))),
DEF("test:re_want",
    K(S1(S2(A("PartyIsDormant"), S2(S1(A("p1")), S1(A("c2"))))))),
DEF("test:re_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:rc_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:re_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:re_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_ext",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:re_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:re_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-ext.db")))))),
"AN AGGREGATE GROUPED BY TWO ROLES OF ITS HEAD IS READ, IN MEMORY AND IN THE DATABASE (Halpin: Dept employs academics of Rank in Quantity iff Quantity = count each Academic who has Rank and works for Dept). test:rule_agg2 reads one readings file: Log Entry has Federation, is in Time Window and has Latency, and two ternaries fully derived, Federation has Error Count for Time Window iff Error Count is the count of Log Entry where that Log Entry has that Federation and that Log Entry is in that Time Window, and Federation has Total Latency for Time Window iff Total Latency is the sum of Latency1 where Log Entry1 has Federation and Log Entry1 is in Time Window and Log Entry1 has Latency1, each grouped by the Federation and the Time Window. e1 and e2 are fA`s in w1 with 10 and 20, e3 fA`s in w2 with 5, e4 fB`s in w1 with 7: the counts are 2, 1 and 1 and the totals 30, 5 and 7, in lambda`s read over the cells (derive:on_read) and in the views (test:dq_sql). Run first, before an aggregate took more than one group variable, both rules read to # and the test answered F.",
DEF("test:rg_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("agg2.md"), A("Log Entry(.id) is an entity type.\nFederation(.id) is an entity type.\nTime Window is a value type.\nLatency is a value type.\n  The data type of Latency is integer.\nError Count is a value type.\n  The data type of Error Count is integer.\nTotal Latency is a value type.\n  The data type of Total Latency is integer.\nLog Entry has Federation.\n  Each Log Entry has at most one Federation.\nLog Entry is in Time Window.\n  Each Log Entry, Time Window combination occurs at most once in the population of Log Entry is in Time Window.\nLog Entry has Latency.\n  Each Log Entry has at most one Latency.\nFederation has Error Count for Time Window. *\n  For each Federation and Time Window, that Federation has at most one Error Count for that Time Window.\n* Federation has Error Count for Time Window iff Error Count is the count of Log Entry where that Log Entry has that Federation and that Log Entry is in that Time Window.\nFederation has Total Latency for Time Window. *\n  For each Federation and Time Window, that Federation has at most one Total Latency for that Time Window.\n* Federation has Total Latency for Time Window iff Total Latency is the sum of Latency1 where Log Entry1 has Federation and Log Entry1 is in Time Window and Log Entry1 has Latency1.\nLog Entry 'e1' has Federation 'fA'.\nLog Entry 'e2' has Federation 'fA'.\nLog Entry 'e3' has Federation 'fA'.\nLog Entry 'e4' has Federation 'fB'.\nLog Entry 'e1' is in Time Window 'w1'.\nLog Entry 'e2' is in Time Window 'w1'.\nLog Entry 'e3' is in Time Window 'w2'.\nLog Entry 'e4' is in Time Window 'w1'.\nLog Entry 'e1' has Latency '10'.\nLog Entry 'e2' has Latency '20'.\nLog Entry 'e3' has Latency '5'.\nLog Entry 'e4' has Latency '7'.\n"), A("agg2/agg2.md"))))),
DEF("test:rg_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rg_files"))),
DEF("test:rg_want",
    K(S2(S2(A("FederationHasErrorCountForTimeWindow"), S3(S3(A("fA"), A("2"), A("w1")), S3(A("fA"), A("1"), A("w2")), S3(A("fB"), A("1"), A("w1")))), S2(A("FederationHasTotalLatencyForTimeWindow"), S3(S3(A("fA"), A("30"), A("w1")), S3(A("fA"), A("5"), A("w2")), S3(A("fB"), A("7"), A("w1"))))))),
DEF("test:rg_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ra_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rg_want"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:rg_cells")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:rule_agg2",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:rg_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:rg_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), K(A("law-rule-agg2.db")))))),
