"test:fact_reflect holds the Facts a store reflects to literal rows, and feeds them to an investigation. Sherlock is independent of the facts, and may be fed any fact set to induce the answer to a query. The store holds three asserted facts, Julia Stoner died unexplained, the ventilator connects her bedroom to the study, and Enoch Drebber was poisoned, and the selection fed is the first two fact types. reflect:facts answers each row of the selection as the Fact of instances.md and nothing else: the Fact is of its Fact Type, fills each Role of it, and the RoleInstance of each, the pair spelled as every objectified instance is, uses the value the row holds at that position. A Fact is spelled as an Event is spelled less its time (store:ev_spell), the fact type, a colon, and each position=value joined by a bar. Then the rule of a literal readings fixture of the Sherlock shape, a Case observes an Observation that is of a Fact and proposes a Hypothesis that expects a Fact Type, is read by the reader and evaluated over the case rows and the reflected Facts: the case corroborates the trained snake, whose fact type the fed set holds, and not the gypsies, whose observation is of a fact outside the selection. Run first with reflect:facts answering nothing, it failed (fact-reflect -> F).",
DEF("test:fr_store",
    K(S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained"), S1(S1(A("Julia Stoner")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom"), S1(S3(A("the ventilator"), A("her bedroom"), A("the study")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonWasPoisoned"), S1(S1(A("Enoch Drebber"))))))),
DEF("test:fr_facts",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:facts"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("PersonDiedUnexplained"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom"))), A("test:fr_store")))),
DEF("test:fr_text",
    K(S2(A("fr.md"), A("Case(.Name) is an entity type.\nObservation(.Title) is an entity type.\nHypothesis(.Claim) is an entity type.\nFact(.Fact Id) is an entity type.\nFact Type(.Fact Type Name) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\nTitle is a value type.\nClaim is a value type.\nFact Id is a value type.\nFact Type Name is a value type.\n\nCase observes Observation.\nObservation is of Fact.\nCase proposes Hypothesis.\nFact is of Fact Type.\nHypothesis expects Fact Type.\n\nCase corroborates Hypothesis. *\n\n* Case corroborates Hypothesis iff that Case proposes that Hypothesis and that Case observes some Observation and that Observation is of some Fact and that Fact is of some Fact Type and that Hypothesis expects that Fact Type.\n")))),
DEF("test:fr_case",
    K(S4(
       S2(A("CaseObservesObservation"), S3(S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the unexplained death")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the ventilator passage")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the poisoning")))),
       S2(A("ObservationIsOfFact"), S3(S2(A("the unexplained death"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained:1=Julia Stoner")), S2(A("the ventilator passage"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study")), S2(A("the poisoning"), A("PersonWasPoisoned:1=Enoch Drebber")))),
       S2(A("CaseProposesHypothesis"), S2(S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("a trained snake killed her")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the gypsies killed her")))),
       S2(A("HypothesisExpectsFactType"), S2(S2(A("a trained snake killed her"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom")), S2(A("the gypsies killed her"), A("PersonWasPoisoned"))))))),
DEF("test:fr_rule",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:find_desc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("CaseCorroboratesHypothesis")),
       S6(A("COMP"), A("read:state_rpaths"), A("read:x_full"), A("read:x_of"), A("compile:text_rows"), A("test:fr_text"))))),
DEF("test:fact_reflect",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FactIsOfFactType")), A("test:fr_facts"))),
          K(S2(S2(A("PersonDiedUnexplained:1=Julia Stoner"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FactFillsRole")), A("test:fr_facts"))),
          K(S4(S2(A("PersonDiedUnexplained:1=Julia Stoner"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained.1")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.1")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.2")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.3")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("RoleInstanceUsesObjectTypeInstance")), A("test:fr_facts"))),
          K(S4(S2(A("PersonDiedUnexplained:1=Julia Stoner.PersonDiedUnexplained.1"), A("Julia Stoner")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study.FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.1"), A("the ventilator")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study.FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.2"), A("her bedroom")), S2(A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study.FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom.3"), A("the study")))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:fr_rule")), K(A("F")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S5(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("derive:eval")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), A("test:fr_rule")), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:fr_case"), A("test:fr_facts")))))),
             K(S1(S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("a trained snake killed her")))))))))),

DEF("test:model_rules",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:targets"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("derive"),
                S3(A("CONS"), A("rules:model"), S2(A("CONST"), PHI())))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:targets"), A("rules:model"))))),

DEF("test:all",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:report")))
,
"A NAME DECLARED IN TWO DOMAINS AT ONE LEVEL IS SAID, AND BOTH DOMAINS ARE NAMED. Namespacing is done by domain, not by hacking up the name: domains provide the namespace. core.md declares that each Function belongs to at most one Domain and has at most one Local Name, and that for each Domain and Local Name at most one Function belongs to that Domain and has that Local Name. The reader recorded a file`s Domain only against the types that file declares, read an instance sentence with no file at all, and reflect:fbd_first kept the first Domain of an id and dropped the others without a word. test:local_names reads three files, two at one level and one at another: fx/a.md and fx/b.md each declare Gizmo, under the Domains alpha and beta, and each says that Widget `w1` is labeled; gx/c.md declares Gizmo under gamma. Over what compile:check answers for them, state:localnames holds <name, Domain, noun, level> for each of the three declarations of Gizmo and for the instance w1 in each file at fx/; the findings name exactly one collision, Gizmo, and its Domains are alpha and beta -- w1 is one Widget spoken of in two files, and gamma is at another level, which the cascade resolves; and the arm reflect:arms gives FunctionHasLocalName answers <Gizmo, Gizmo> over those cells. Before the reader records any of it, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:ln_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'beta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/b.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("gx/c.md"))))),
"<name, text, path>: the file`s pair as compile:file_pair makes it from the file it reads.",
DEF("test:ln_pair",
    S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:domain_fault"), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:pair_of_rows"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:text_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2)))), N(3)))),
"<cells, findings> of test:ln_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:ln_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ln_files")))),
DEF("test:ln_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:localnames")), N(1)))),
DEF("test:ln_coll",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("collision")))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))), N(2))),
DEF("test:ln_arm",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionHasLocalName")), A("reflect:arms")))),
DEF("test:ln_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(1))),
DEF("test:local_names",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S9(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("alpha"), A("Object Type"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("beta"), A("Object Type"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("gamma"), A("Object Type"), A("gx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("w1"), A("alpha"), A("Widget"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("w1"), A("beta"), A("Widget"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:ln_coll")), K(S1(A("Gizmo"))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:ln_coll")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(4), N(1), A("test:ln_coll")), K(S2(A("alpha"), A("beta")))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:ln_arm")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Gizmo"), A("Gizmo"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ln_arm"), A("test:ln_store"))))))),
       A("test:ln_run")))),
"<store>: the composed store with LawPrSrc, a Thing with a Basis, asserted; LawPrOwn and LawPrFed, a Thing with a Value, each marked + and derived as the projection of LawPrSrc, unique on the Thing; and LawPrFed federated at the JSON Path law-pr-value.",
DEF("test:pr_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
                K(S2(A("state:fts"), S3(
                   S5(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI())))))),
             K(S2(A("state:declared"), S3(
                S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis"))),
                S2(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value"))),
                S2(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")))))))),
          K(S2(A("state:derived"), S2(S2(A("LawPrOwn"), A("semi")), S2(A("LawPrFed"), A("semi"))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:rules"), S2(
          S3(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPrSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))),
          S3(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPrSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))))))))),
"The asserted rows of the fixture, each <fact type, row>: law-pr-k1 with the Basis law-pr-b1, law-pr-k2 with law-pr-b2, and LawPrFed federated at law-pr-value.",
DEF("test:pr_rows",
    K(S3(
       S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1"))),
       S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2"))),
       S2(A("FactTypeIsFederatedAtJSONPath"), S2(A("LawPrFed"), A("law-pr-value")))))),
"<store>: the fixture, its rows put over its schema and closed from it as a write closes, so the rules give LawPrOwn and LawPrFed law-pr-b1 for law-pr-k1 and law-pr-b2 for law-pr-k2.",
DEF("test:pr_fx",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:closed_from"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("INSERT"), A("test:dft_put")), A("apndr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("reverse"), A("test:pr_rows")), A("id"))))),
       A("test:pr_schema"))),
"<name, store> to the rows the store holds of the fact type, not the rows a read of it answers: its top-level cell, else its descriptor`s (derive:raw_rows), and its cell in FILE.",
