"A SYNC REPLACES AN ENTERED VALUE OF A FEDERATED + FACT TYPE, AND NOTHING DERIVED REPLACES ONE THE USER OWNS. A sync from an external federation is a derivation; for a federated fact type an entered value is a write-through to the system and the next sync replaces it; for one the user owns, not federated, an entered value is never overwritten. A fact type is federated where the store declares it federated at a JSON Path or a Function yields it. Over test:pr_both, where law-pr-e3 is entered for law-pr-k3 in LawPrFed, federated, and in LawPrOwn, not, a sync of a page that reads law-pr-s3 for law-pr-k3 in both: the store no longer holds the entered row of LawPrFed, and a read screen shows the page`s fact for it (fed:shown_fact), a + fact type being read through and not cached; while LawPrOwn still answers law-pr-e3 for law-pr-k3 and not the page`s law-pr-s3; and each still answers what its rule derives, law-pr-b1 for law-pr-k1, entered and derived rows being one union (core.md:380-382 and 395-397). An entered row overrides nothing, and the Thing`s uniqueness refuses an entry for law-pr-k1, which the rule derives law-pr-b1 for (test:pr_refused), so the law enters for law-pr-k3, which the rule derives nothing for, and the derived row is read beside the entered one.",
