"A READ OF A ++ DERIVED FACT TYPE IS WHAT WAS ENTERED UNITED WITH WHAT ITS RULES DERIVE, AND ONLY WHAT WAS ENTERED IS STORED. Over test:pp_fx, after a fact POST of law-pp-e3 for law-pp-k3 in LawPpOwn: a read of LawPpOwn answers law-pp-e3 for law-pp-k3 and the derived law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1 and law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2, and nothing else; the store holds the entered row and neither derived row; and a fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1, which the rule derives law-pp-b1 for, is refused by the Thing`s uniqueness, 409 (test:ppx_refused). A ++ fact type is semi-derived as a + one is: what was entered of it united with what its rules derive, an entered row overriding nothing (core.md:380-382 and 395-397), and its storage decides when a derivation runs, never what it answers, nothing evaluating eagerly (core.md:391-394: no write stores a derived row). So the law enters for law-pp-k3, a key the rule derives nothing for, and a value for law-pp-k1 is refused by the Thing`s uniqueness. Run first, it failed: a ++ fact type was read as its rules alone, and a write stored the rows its rules derived as entered.",
DEF("test:plusplus_entered",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ppx_union"), A("test:ppx_refused")))),
"AN INPUT THAT MOVES RE-DERIVES ON READ WHAT A ++ DERIVED FACT TYPE`S RULE DERIVES, AND LEAVES WHAT WAS ENTERED. Over test:pp_entered, after the Basis of law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc moves from law-pp-b2 to law-pp-b3 (a fact DELETE, then a fact POST): a read of LawPpOwn answers law-pp-e3 for law-pp-k3, still the entered value, law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1, and law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2, derived again, and nothing else; and the store holds the entered row alone, neither the old law-pp-b2 nor the new law-pp-b3 nor law-pp-b1, so no stored row differs from what the rules derive (core.md:391-394). A ++ fact type is semi-derived as a + one is: what was entered of it united with what its rules derive, an entered row overriding nothing (core.md:380-382 and 395-397), and its storage decides when a derivation runs, never what it answers, nothing evaluating eagerly (core.md:391-394: no write stores a derived row). So the law enters for law-pp-k3, a key the rule derives nothing for, and a value for law-pp-k1 is refused by the Thing`s uniqueness. Run first, it failed: a ++ fact type was read as its rules alone, and a write stored the rows its rules derived as entered.",
