"test:kept_judged holds the in-place compile`s judged store to the tables it leaves in the store (on a large app`s store, a judged store lacking every Agent Chat`s user, mode and time and every Completion`s text and time shows 34 false mandatory violations, alethic_clean F). The fixture is Crate, identified by its Name, with exactly one Weight each, two Crates: its tables laid out and filled in a database through the storage interface, Crate`s table listed as left in the store (storage:kept_open), and the store the closure would answer without the facts of that table, Crate has Weight empty -- which the judge alone finds in violation of the mandatory. compile:ip_judged of the database and that store holds every Crate`s Weight and the judge answers no alethic violation; the database is cleared after. Run first with compile:ip_judged answering the store it is given, it failed.",
