"test:uc_spanning holds that the uniqueness arm of a write`s validation computes the population of a fact type only when a uniqueness over it can fail. A uniqueness over every role of its fact type holds of any population, which is a set (cmd:viol_for finds none such), so a fact type whose every uniqueness spans its roles, or which has none, has nothing for the arm to check. Over test:uc_fx, told the write moved Operation is overridable, a unary whose one uniqueness spans its one role, and UcPair, unique per Function, ui:vi_ucs hands the arm UcPair`s descriptor alone. On a copy of a large app`s store a create of one entity computed a unary marked + computed on read for 1.4 s, to check a uniqueness that cannot fail. Run first, the arm had no such list (unresolved atom ui:vi_ucs).",
