"<answer, <fact type, rows>> to T when the store the write answer carries holds those rows of the fact type and no other.",
DEF("test:drd_only",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2))))),
"<store> to what a fact DELETE of law-drd-f1 in LawDrdHas answers over the fixture.",
DEF("test:drd_ra",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:drd_fx"), K(A("LawDrdHas")), K(S1(A("law-drd-f1")))))),
"<store> to what a fact DELETE of law-drd-f1 under law-drd-e1 in LawDrdUnder answers over the fixture.",
DEF("test:drd_rb",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:drd_fx"), K(A("LawDrdUnder")), K(S2(A("law-drd-f1"), A("law-drd-e1")))))),
"<store> to <the fixture, what a fact DELETE of law-drd-f2 under law-drd-e2 in LawDrdUnder answers over it>.",
DEF("test:drd_rc",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawDrdUnder")), K(S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-e2")))))), A("test:drd_fx"))),
"A RETRACT OF A ROW A PROJECTION DERIVES RETRACTS ITS ONE SOURCE. A derived fact is specifically meant for views, otherwise the direct facts would do, and a retract of a derivation retracts its source facts. Over test:drd_fx, LawDrdHas is derived and stored as the projection of LawDrdIn on its Function, and law-drd-f1 is in law-drd-d1 alone: a fact DELETE of law-drd-f1 in LawDrdHas commits (201), after which LawDrdIn holds law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 no longer, LawDrdHas no longer holds law-drd-f1 and still holds law-drd-f2, and LawDrdIn holds the two rows of law-drd-f2 and no other. Before main:dr_plan the retract took the derived fact type row alone, and the source stayed.",
DEF("test:derived_retract_proj",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(N(201)))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(A("law-drd-f1"), A("law-drd-d1")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdHas"), S1(A("law-drd-f1")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdHas"), S1(A("law-drd-f2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_only"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d2")), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d3")))))))),
       A("test:drd_ra")))),
"A RETRACT OF A ROW A JOIN DERIVES ALONG ONE PATH RETRACTS THE ASSERTED FACTS ON THAT PATH (the rule: a row derived through a join retracts every asserted fact on its derivation path that no other derivation of the same row survives without). Over test:drd_fx, law-drd-f1 is under law-drd-e1 along one path, law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 and law-drd-d1 under law-drd-e1: a fact DELETE of that row of LawDrdUnder commits (201), after which LawDrdIn holds law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 no longer, LawDrdSub holds law-drd-d1 under law-drd-e1 no longer, LawDrdUnder no longer holds law-drd-f1 under law-drd-e1 and still holds law-drd-f2 under law-drd-e2, and LawDrdIn and LawDrdSub hold their other two rows each and no other. Before main:dr_plan the retract took the derived fact type row alone, and both sources stayed.",
DEF("test:derived_retract_join",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(N(201)))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(A("law-drd-f1"), A("law-drd-d1")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdSub"), S2(A("law-drd-d1"), A("law-drd-e1")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdUnder"), S2(A("law-drd-f1"), A("law-drd-e1")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdUnder"), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-e2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_only"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d2")), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d3"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_only"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdSub"), S2(S2(A("law-drd-d2"), A("law-drd-e2")), S2(A("law-drd-d3"), A("law-drd-e2")))))))),
       A("test:drd_rb")))),
"A RETRACT OF A ROW DERIVED ALONG TWO PATHS THAT SHARE NO FACT IS REFUSED, NAMING THE FACTS, AND NOTHING IS GUESSED. Over test:drd_fx, law-drd-f2 is under law-drd-e2 along two paths, through law-drd-d2 and through law-drd-d3, and no asserted fact is on both: a fact DELETE of that row of LawDrdUnder answers refused (409); the answer carries the store it was given; and its body is the refusal with the four candidate facts, each <fact type, row>, in the order of their JSON: law-drd-f2 in law-drd-d2 and in law-drd-d3, and law-drd-d2 and law-drd-d3 under law-drd-e2. Before main:dr_plan the retract committed and took the derived fact type row alone.",
DEF("test:derived_retract_ambiguous",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), K(N(409)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:dw_same"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(1))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("render:json"), K(S3(A("refused"), A("retract refused: the row is derived along more than one path and no fact is on every one, so which facts to retract is not determined; retract one of these instead"), S4(
          S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d2"))),
          S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d3"))),
          S2(A("LawDrdSub"), S2(A("law-drd-d2"), A("law-drd-e2"))),
          S2(A("LawDrdSub"), S2(A("law-drd-d3"), A("law-drd-e2")))))))))),
       A("test:drd_rc")))),
"<store>: the composed store marking three derived fact types, LawNvView derived on query (*), LawNvKept derived and stored (**) and LawNvEntered semi-derived (+); LawNvSaid is marked nothing, so it is asserted.",
DEF("test:nvm_fx",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
       K(S2(A("state:derived"), S3(S2(A("LawNvView"), A("full")), S2(A("LawNvKept"), A("derived-and-stored")), S2(A("LawNvEntered"), A("semi-derived")))))))),
"<tree> to the items of its menus: every element after the head of each section, an atom or the empty header of the layer yielding none.",
DEF("test:nvm_items",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), A("atom"), K(PHI()), S4(A("COND"), A("null"), K(PHI()), A("tl")))))),
"<store> to the items of the root menu the store answers, at no App.",
DEF("test:nvm_root",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_items"), A("ui:root"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI())))),
"<items> to T when the root holds LawNvView as an item, the collection link of its own address, and holds none for LawNvKept, LawNvEntered or LawNvSaid.",
DEF("test:nvm_menu",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvView"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvView")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvKept"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvKept")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvEntered"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvEntered")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvSaid"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvSaid")))), A("id")))))),
"<<store, resource>, methods> to T when the perspectives the map offers the resource over the store are those methods.",
DEF("test:nvm_offers",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("nav:perspectives"), N(1)), N(2)))),
"THE CONTROLS THE MAP OFFERS FOLLOW THE MARKER. links(e) = nav(e) union transitions(status(e)) offers per fact type what its derivation marker admits: an asserted fact type GET, POST, PUT and DELETE; a derived fact type derived on query (*) or derived and stored (**) GET, and a DELETE that retracts the facts its row is derived from, and no POST or PUT, since its rule owns its rows; a semi-derived fact type (+ or ++) GET, and POST, PUT and DELETE on the values entered, a DELETE restoring the derived default. And a derived fact type derived on query is a view group in the menu: its own collection link, read-only, though no table holds it. Over test:nvm_fx: nav:perspectives offers LawNvSaid GET, POST, PUT and DELETE, LawNvView and LawNvKept GET and DELETE, and LawNvEntered GET, POST, PUT and DELETE; the actions of the collection page at LawNvView hold no Add, and those at Function hold its Add as before; and the root at no App lists LawNvView as an item and none of the other three. Expected before the change to fail (nav-markers -> F): the map named every method of http:method_kinds for every resource, every collection page offered Add, and the root listed only the tables of the relational map.",
DEF("test:nav_markers",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvSaid"))), K(S4(A("GET"), A("POST"), A("PUT"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvView"))), K(S2(A("GET"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvKept"))), K(S2(A("GET"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvEntered"))), K(S4(A("GET"), A("POST"), A("PUT"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:coll_actions"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("LawNvView"))))), K(S2(A("actions"), A(""))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:coll_actions"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("Function"))))), K(S3(A("actions"), A(""), S4(A("button"), A("+ new"), S2(A("new"), A("Function")), A("Add")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_menu"), A("test:nvm_root"))),
       A("test:nvm_fx")))),
"A FULLY DERIVED FACT TYPE IS A VIEW. CLAUDE.md, the application flow: a derived fact type is a view. test:derived_view reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does: Member joins Club and Club holds Venue are asserted, each many to many, and Member attends Venue is marked * and derived by joining the two. Over the store those cells make, the relational map lays out no table for the derived fact type and rmap:ddl emits CREATE VIEW for it; and through the storage interface -- storage:fresh, storage:schema, storage:put of compile:tables, then storage:columns and storage:rows of the derived fact type -- the view answers exactly the rows derive:on_read derives, which are not none. The database is law-derived-view.db beside the process, made fresh before and cleared after.",
DEF("test:dv_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("views.md"), A("Member(.id) is an entity type.\nClub(.id) is an entity type.\nVenue(.id) is an entity type.\nMember joins Club.\n  Each Member, Club combination occurs at most once in the population of Member joins Club.\nClub holds Venue.\n  Each Club, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Club holds Venue.\nMember attends Venue. *\n  Each Member, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Member attends Venue.\n* Member attends Venue iff Member joins Club and that Club holds Venue.\nMember 'ann' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'cy' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'bob' joins Club 'go'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'york'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'leeds'.\nClub 'go' holds Venue 'hull'.\nClub 'rowing' holds Venue 'ely'.\n"), A("fx/views.md"))))),
"The store test:dv_files makes: the cells compile:check answers for it, each chunked as a compile files it (compile:cellify).",
DEF("test:dv_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:dv_files"))),
DEF("test:dv_dft",
    K(A("MemberAttendsVenue"))),
DEF("test:dv_db",
    K(A("law-derived-view.db"))),
"<store> to <store, database>, the database made fresh.",
DEF("test:dv_s1",
    S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), A("test:dv_db")))),
"<store, database> to <store, database, script>: the relational map laid out in the database.",
DEF("test:dv_s2",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:schema"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(1))))),
"<store, database, script> to <store, database, counts>: every table the map lays out filled with its rows, as a compile fills them.",
DEF("test:dv_s3",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:sb_put_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:tables"), N(1)), N(2)))))),
"<store, database, ...> to the columns the database gives the derived fact type, none when it has no relation of that name.",
DEF("test:dv_cols",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:columns"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), A("test:dv_dft")))),
"<store, database, ...> to the rows the database answers for the derived fact type.",
DEF("test:dv_rows",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:dv_cols")), K(PHI()), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:rows"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), A("test:dv_dft"), A("test:dv_cols"))))),
"<store, database, counts> to <store, database, tables, derived fact type rows>.",
DEF("test:dv_s4",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:tables"), N(2)), A("test:dv_rows"))),
"<store, database, tables, derived fact type rows> to <store, tables, derived fact type rows, database>, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:dv_s5",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(1), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2)))),
"<store, ...> to the rows the derivation derives for the derived fact type.",
DEF("test:dv_derived",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dv_dft"), N(1)))),
"<store, tables, derived fact type rows, database> to T when the database holds no table of the derived fact type, the script creates a view of it, the derivation derives some rows of it, and the view answers exactly those.",
DEF("test:dv_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dv_dft"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), N(2)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:ddl"), N(1)), K(A("CREATE VIEW \"MemberAttendsVenue\"")))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("test:dv_derived")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(3), A("test:dv_derived")))))),
DEF("test:derived_view",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:dv_verdict"), S6(A("COMP"), A("test:dv_s5"), A("test:dv_s4"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), A("test:dv_s1")), A("test:dv_store"))),
"<store>: transitions of one event, <from, event, to>, with no guards: c1 to cT and cT to pDone, a to b and b to c, x to y and y to x.",
DEF("test:sc_trs",
    K(S6(S3(A("c1"), A("e"), A("cT")), S3(A("cT"), A("e"), A("pDone")), S3(A("a"), A("e"), A("b")), S3(A("b"), A("e"), A("c")), S3(A("x"), A("e"), A("y")), S3(A("y"), A("e"), A("x"))))),
"A SUB-MACHINE THAT ENDS CARRIES ITS EVENT ON. test:step_completes holds store:sc_run to test:sc_trs over the composed store, the ends being cT, x and y. From cT, which ends a sub-machine, the event goes on to pDone; from b, which ends nothing, it stays at b; from y it goes on to x and stops there, since x would take it back to y, where it stood. Run first with no Status counted an end, it failed (step-completes -> F).",
DEF("test:step_completes",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("cT")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("pDone")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("b")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("b")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("y")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("x"))))))),
"<store>: the composed store with a sub-machine law-open of law-sr defining law-received, which law-accept exits there, and law-merged, which only law-sr`s law-close exits. The Status law-open of law-sr has the sub-machine law-open (Status has sub-machine State Machine Definition), the one name for the composite and the machine.",
DEF("test:ea_fx",
    S(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-open"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusIsInitialInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-received"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-accept"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionIsFromStatus")), K(S2(A("law-accept"), A("law-received"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionIsToStatus")), K(S2(A("law-accept"), A("law-merged"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusIsInitialInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-open"), A("law-sr"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-close"), A("law-sr"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionIsFromStatus")), K(S2(A("law-close"), A("law-merged"))))),
       A("id"))),
"A STATUS ENDS A SUB-MACHINE WHEN NOTHING OF THE SUB-MACHINE LEAVES IT. test:end_at holds store:sc_end_at over test:ea_fx: law-merged ends law-open, which law-sr defines and which nothing exits it in; law-received does not, law-accept exiting it in law-open; and law-open, a Status of law-sr, ends nothing, law-sr being the sub-machine of no Status. Run first with every machine counted a sub-machine, it failed (end-at -> F), law-open answering.",
DEF("test:end_at",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-merged")), A("test:ea_fx"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-received")), A("test:ea_fx"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-open")), A("test:ea_fx")))))),
"A MACHINE IS A STATUS ONLY BY NESTING. State machines must be defined correctly. state.md read `State Machine Definition is a subtype of Status`, so every machine was a Status, and a top-level one, which no Transition reaches, stood against core.md`s `For each Status, some Transition is from that Status or some Transition is to that Status`. It reads now `Status has sub-machine State Machine Definition`, each State Machine Definition the sub-machine of at most one Status. test:sub_machine holds the reader and the machine over test:sm_files, a literal readings file: Ticket, a top-level machine whose Status Open has the sub-machine Review, where approve takes Draft to Approved, and Note, another top-level machine. The reader files Open has sub-machine Review with the uniqueness on the role of the machine; no machine is among the Statuses; the inclusive-or the file states is read, and every Status is the from or the to of some Transition. Approved ends a sub-machine, the end of Review, and neither Draft, which approve leaves there, nor Closed nor Read, Statuses of top-level machines, does (store:sc_end_at); entering Open enters Draft (main:enter); the machine for Ticket nests Review and not Note (main:noun_smds_all), and resolve, which leaves Open, leaves Draft and Approved too (main:machine_trs). Run first, with lambda reading a machine as a Status of the same name, it failed (sub-machine -> F): Approved ended nothing, Open entered itself, and Ticket nested nothing.",
DEF("test:sm_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("sm.md"), A("Status(.Name) is an entity type.\nState Machine Definition(.Name) is an entity type.\nTransition(.Name) is an entity type.\nEvent Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance(.Name) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\n\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nState Machine Definition is for Object Type.\nStatus has sub-machine State Machine Definition.\n  For each State Machine Definition, at most one Status has sub-machine that State Machine Definition.\nStatus is initial in State Machine Definition.\nStatus is defined in State Machine Definition.\nTransition is defined in State Machine Definition.\nTransition is from- Status.\nTransition is to- Status.\nTransition is triggered by Event Type.\nTransition exits Status in State Machine Definition.\n\nFor each Status, some Transition is from that Status or some Transition is to that Status.\n\nState Machine Definition 'Ticket' is for Object Type 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Closed' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nTransition 'resolve' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nTransition 'resolve' is from Status 'Open'.\nTransition 'resolve' is to Status 'Closed'.\nTransition 'resolve' is triggered by Event Type 'Resolves'.\nTransition 'resolve' exits Status 'Open' in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' has sub-machine State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Draft' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Draft' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Approved' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nTransition 'approve' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nTransition 'approve' is from Status 'Draft'.\nTransition 'approve' is to Status 'Approved'.\nTransition 'approve' is triggered by Event Type 'Approves'.\nTransition 'approve' exits Status 'Draft' in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nState Machine Definition 'Note' is for Object Type 'Note'.\nStatus 'Unread' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nStatus 'Unread' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nStatus 'Read' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nTransition 'read' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nTransition 'read' is from Status 'Unread'.\nTransition 'read' is to Status 'Read'.\nTransition 'read' is triggered by Event Type 'Reads'.\nTransition 'read' exits Status 'Unread' in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\n"), A("smx/sm.md"))))),
"<any>: the cells compile:check answers for test:sm_files, as a store (test:ln_store).",
DEF("test:sm_cells",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ln_store"),
       S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:sm_files"))))),
"<cells>: the cells with each fact type`s rows as a population cell of its own, where a machine reads them (system:pop_rows).",
DEF("test:sm_store_of",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), N(5)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))),
       A("id")))),
"<cells, store> to the Statuses the readings populate: the instances Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type gives Status (state:otpops is gone; the instance list of a type is a view of the classification, and test:sm_files declares the classification so the reader reflects it, as instances.md does for an app).",
DEF("test:sm_statuses",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Status")))), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)), K(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType")), N(2)))))),
"<cells, store> to the rows <from, event, to> the machine for Ticket fires, with the machines nested in it.",
DEF("test:sm_trs",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:machine_trs"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket"))))),
DEF("test:sub_machine",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"),
       S(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition")), N(2))), K(S1(S2(A("Open"), A("Review")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:in:StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition#2")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:ucs")), N(1)))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Ticket"), A("Note"), A("Review"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Ticket"), A("Note"), A("Review"))), A("test:sm_statuses")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("DJ:e:TransitionIsFromStatus#2+TransitionIsToStatus#2")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:djmands")), N(1)))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sm_statuses"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"),
                S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("TransitionIsFromStatus")), N(2)))),
                S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("TransitionIsToStatus")), N(2))))))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Open")), A("test:sm_statuses"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Approved")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Draft")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Closed")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Read")), N(2))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:enter"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Open")), N(2))), K(A("Draft")))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Review")), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:noun_smds_all"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket")))))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Note")), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:noun_smds_all"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Draft"), A("Resolves"), A("Closed"))), A("test:sm_trs"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Approved"), A("Resolves"), A("Closed"))), A("test:sm_trs")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:sm_store_of")), A("test:sm_cells")))),
"A VALUE THE READINGS ENUMERATE IS ONE THEY INTRODUCE. test:enum_introduces holds compile:ip_gone over literal rows: of the instances the last readings introduced (law ep, law-i0, law-i1), the new readings introduce law-i1 by an instance sentence and law ep as one of a value type`s possible values, so law-i0 alone is gone. Run first with compile:ip_r1typed reading instance sentences only, it failed (enum-introduces -> F), law ep answering gone.",
