    S3(A("COMP"), A("store:cl_put"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), K(A("state:deontics")), S3(A("COMP"), A("apndl"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(S3(A("DEO:m:GadgetIsInvolvedInGadgetHasPart#1"), A("mandatory"), S1(S2(A("GadgetIsInvolvedInGadgetHasPart"), N(1)))))), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:deontics")), A("id"))), K(A("#")))), K(PHI()), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:deontics")), A("id"))))))), A("id")))),
"AN OBLIGATION IS CHECKED, OR THE LAW SAYS WHICH IS NOT (every deontic must work). Over the composed store no obligation row names a fact type the check cannot read; over test:du_link, whose one more row is keyed and legged by a link as every obligation over an objectified or many-to-many fact type was, test:deo_unread answers that row. Such rows are DEO:m:SchemaDesignIsInvolvedInUserApprovesSchemaDesign#1 and DEO:m:StateMachineDefinitionIsInvolvedInStatusIsTerminalInStateMachineDefinition#1, which every resident app`s carriers can hold, and more on a large app`s store.",
