"AN ENTITY RETRACT NAMED FOR NO COLLECTION FINDS THE ONE HOLDING ITS ID (main:re_group): an id that is an instance of a collection resolves to it whatever type the row names, and an id that is nobody`s resolves to none, which the retract refuses as before.",
DEF("test:re_group",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:re_group"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(S2(A("Some Subtype"), A("x-law-rg")))), A("test:rg_fx"))), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), A("ui:groups")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:re_group"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(S2(A("Some Subtype"), A("no-such-law-id")))), A("id"))), K(A(""))))))),
"<store>: test:sp_a2 holding the two rows the reflection keeps of dc-law-step and its machine: it is currently in Under Review, and its machine is an instance of the Domain Change definition.",
DEF("test:rd_fx",
    S4(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus")), K(S2(A("dc-law-step"), A("step2-populate"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StateMachineIsInstanceOfStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("sm.dc-law-step"), A("CSDP"))))),
       A("test:sp_a2"))),
"A RETRACT LEAVES NO ROW OF THE ENTITY IN A DERIVED FACT TYPE THE STORE KEEPS (main:re_names). Over test:rd_fx, the entity DELETE of dc-law-step answers 201, and neither ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus holds a row of dc-law-step nor StateMachineIsInstanceOfStateMachineDefinition one of sm.dc-law-step: the rows a retract can leave behind. Seen to fail with main:re_names answering the declared fact types alone.",
