    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_entity_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("Function")), K(S1(A("law-sdr-2")))))),
"A RETRACT TAKES BACK WHAT A STORED DERIVATION DERIVED FROM IT. `**` columns store the derivation and updates, but do not accept overrides, and retracting a fact is just writing a null to the columns related to that fact. A `**` derived fact type is derived on update (Halpin and Morgan 2008, pp. 100-101): stored, and recomputed whenever its defining facts change, a retraction included. Over test:sdr_fx, whose LawSdrProper and LawSdrMost are derived and stored from the asserted LawSdrIn and LawSdrSub as instances.md derives Object Type Instance is properly of and is most specifically of Object Type: the closure holds law-sdr-1 properly of Message and most specifically of Response, and law-sdr-2 most specifically of Message; (A) a fact DELETE of law-sdr-1 as an instance of Response commits, after which law-sdr-1 is properly of nothing and most specifically of Message, and law-sdr-2 is still most specifically of Message; (B) an entity DELETE of law-sdr-2 commits, after which law-sdr-2 is most specifically of nothing, and law-sdr-1 keeps both its rows.",
DEF("test:stored_retract",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), A("test:sdr_checks"), A("test:sdr_fx"))),
"<fixture> to the four verdicts of test:stored_retract.",
