"A RECIPE RETRACTS MANY ENTITIES IN ONE STEP. Retiring thousands of Observations is one step, where a retract that takes one id is thousands of steps. The entity DELETE takes a query recipe where the id stood, the recipe language of the served query verb, and retracts whole every entity whose id the first column of an answered row holds, all in one step validated once, with the cascade and the gates one entity`s retract has. Over test:br_fx, three Observations, two of them of a Fact: (A) the retract of the Observations less those of a Fact commits once, 201, and takes obs-law-br3 alone, leaving obs-law-br1 and obs-law-br2 and both their ObservationIsOfFact rows; (B) a recipe that answers no rows retracts nothing and says so, 200, and obs-law-br3 stays.",
