       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:br_has"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("obs-law-br3")), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObservationIsOfFact")), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))), K(S2(S2(A("obs-law-br1"), A("f-law-br1")), S2(A("obs-law-br2"), A("f-law-br2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), K(N(200)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:br_has"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("obs-law-br3")), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(2))))))),
"test:retract_sql holds an entity retract by a recipe to one program the database runs. The fixture is test:br_fx`s shape as an app declares it, so the store lays it out: Observation and Fact, each identified by its Name, Observation is of Fact many to many, and the classification Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type declared beside them as instances.md declares it; obs-rs-1 is of f-rs-1, obs-rs-2 and obs-rs-3 are of none, and the four are classified. (A) One sqlite:program over a database with no file lays the store out and fills it (sqlite:store_script), runs retract:program for test:br_a`s recipe, the Observations less those of a Fact, and reads the two tables back by the recipe language`s own SQL: it commits, obs-rs-1 with its classification and its Observation is of Fact row remains with f-rs-1, and obs-rs-2 and obs-rs-3 are gone. (B) Over a database laid out and filled the same way, the same program with a refuse step after it that answers a row answers refused, and all three Observations remain; the database is cleared after. Run first with retract:program answering no step, it failed.",
DEF("test:rs_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cs_store"), K(S4(A("Name is a value type.\nObject Type Instance(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\n  Each Object Type Instance, Object Type combination occurs at most once in the population of Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nObservation(.Name) is an entity type.\nFact(.Name) is an entity type.\nObservation is of Fact.\n  It is possible that some Observation is of more than one Fact.\n  It is possible that more than one Observation is of the same Fact.\n"),
       S2(S2(A("ObservationIsOfFact"), S1(S2(A("obs-rs-1"), A("f-rs-1")))), S2(A("ObjectTypeIsOfObjectKind"), S4(S2(A("Object Type Instance"), A("entity")), S2(A("Object Type"), A("entity")), S2(A("Observation"), A("entity")), S2(A("Fact"), A("entity"))))),
       S4(S2(A("obs-rs-1"), A("Observation")), S2(A("obs-rs-2"), A("Observation")), S2(A("obs-rs-3"), A("Observation")), S2(A("f-rs-1"), A("Fact"))),
       A("C"))))),
