"test:oti_role_keeps_class: playing a role of Object Type Instance keeps an instance`s class (ORM). Object Type Instance is the population of instances of object types (`Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type`, instances.md), so every typed entity instance already falls under it. Over test:oti_fx, after a fact POST of law-oti-n1 is required orientation and a reflection pass: law-oti-n1 holds the unary, so it is an Object Type Instance for it; it is most specifically a LawOtiNote and nothing else, it is of the Function LawOtiNote, and it belongs to law-oti-notes both as an Object Type Instance and as a Function. MEASURED on a large app`s store, with an instance of a type of its own: after the unary was asserted it was an instance of that type, Function and Object Type Instance, most specifically of that type and Object Type Instance, properly of Function, a Function of the Domain instances, and belonged as an Object Type Instance to no Domain, so orient, which scopes the required orientation by that Domain, never saw it.",
