"test:oti_role_retract_clean: a retract takes what the retracted fact supported. Over test:oti_fx, a fact POST of law-oti-n1 is required orientation and then a fact DELETE of it, each followed by a reflection pass, leave law-oti-n1`s classification rows (test:oti_cls) as they were before the POST, and the fixture`s are not empty: law-oti-n1 is most specifically a LawOtiNote there. MEASURED on a large app`s store: after a unary on an instance was retracted, every row its assertion had added stayed -- the classification under Function and Object Type Instance, the properly-of, most-specifically-of and of-Function rows they gave, and the Domain instances. AND THE CLASSIFICATION THE UNARY LEFT IS RETRACTED WITH WHAT IT SUPPORTED: over test:oti_stray, the store such a POST left, with law-oti-n1 an Object Type Instance and, by the reflection`s closure, a Function, a fact DELETE of law-oti-n1 as an Object Type Instance and a reflection pass leave its classification rows as they were in test:oti_fx. Seen to fail with main:cls_rows taking the cone of the type alone: the Function row stayed, a row nothing but the retracted classification supported, so law-oti-n1 was most specifically a Function.",
DEF("test:oti_role_retract_clean",
