"test:assert_keeps_class: the served assert and create verbs register a filler as a fact POST does, through main:cr_held. Over test:oti_fx: after the assert verb`s DEF asserts law-oti-n1 is required orientation, followed by a reflection pass, test:oti_kept holds: law-oti-n1 holds the unary, is most specifically a LawOtiNote and nothing else, and belongs to law-oti-notes. After the create verb`s DEF creates a row naming law-oti-n1 under its collection, Function, with a Description, and a reflection pass, law-oti-n1 is most specifically a LawOtiNote alone and belongs to law-oti-notes. And an assert that classifies law-oti-n2 a LawOtiNote and asserts it is required orientation in the same step leaves law-oti-n2 holding the unary, most specifically a LawOtiNote alone and of the Domain law-oti-notes. MEASURED on a large app`s store: an assert that several instances are required orientation filed each under Object Type Instance again -- an instance of its own type, Function and Object Type Instance, most specifically of its type and Object Type Instance, a Function of the Domain instances -- where the same unary by fact POST kept its class: main:ab_reg wrote every pair main:ab_pairs named whose exact classification row the store did not hold, and ui:create0 registered a row`s id under its collection through ui:instance_add, neither asking main:cr_held.",
