"THE INSTANCE LIST OF A TYPE IS A VIEW OF THE CLASSIFICATION. A derived fact is specifically meant for views, otherwise the direct facts would do. Over test:cv_fx, a store holding Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type and Object Type is a subtype of Object Type and no other cell -- law-cv-a1 a LawCvAnimal, law-cv-d1 and law-cv-d2 LawCvDogs, law-cv-c1 a LawCvCat, LawCvDog a subtype of LawCvAnimal -- ui:ids answers LawCvAnimal as law-cv-a1, law-cv-d1 and law-cv-d2 (the type and its subtype cone), LawCvDog as its two, LawCvCat as its one, and LawCvBird as nothing. At DERIVED FACT TYPE ui:ids read a second home, the cell state:otpops, which this store does not hold, so the first three answered nothing.",
