       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-otv-1")), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:ids"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:otv_fx"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType")), K(S2(A("law-otv-1"), A("LawOtvSub"))))), K(A("LawOtvSub"))))))))),

"A VALUE BELONGS TO NO DOMAIN. An entity is of the Domain of its most specific type, and a value has no Domain (instances.md). test:value_no_domain derives the Domain of every instance of the composed store whose most specific type is an entity type or a value type, as orient derives an instance`s Domain: its most specific types and the Domains they belong to (orient:rb2, over every Domain the store names; an instance`s Domain is its type`s, by inheritance). It holds when the store has instances whose most specific type is a value type, the derivation answers some rows, and none of those rows is a value`s. An orient that read the value types beside the entity types would give the 387 values of the base store 455 Domain rows of core.",
