"test:facts_moved holds compile:fm_of over law-facts-moved.db, a ledger written to say it. The last readings asserted A x1, A y1 and D q1 and the last closure added D d1, D d2 and E e1; the new readings assert A x1, A z1 and D q1, the closed store holds D d1, D d3, D q1 and D r1 of D, the one fact type its rows are read of, and the runtime wrote D r1. The facts moved are A z1 added and A y1 removed, D d3 added and D d2 removed: D q1 is the readings` and D r1 the runtime`s, so neither moved by the closure, and nothing of E was read, so nothing of it is taken away. The engine keeps the four in _moved, each with its side, for the tables` write. compile:ip_facts_moved_of answers D`s two from an operand holding the set, and <phi, phi> for B, of which nothing moved. The database is made fresh before and cleared after. Run first with the runtime`s facts left in the closure`s rows (sqlite:facts_moved without _fmrt), it failed (facts-moved -> F), D r1 answering added.",
