    S(A("CONS"), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), K(N(0)), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(PHI()))),
"test:kt_left holds the fact types that keep the old store`s read from leaving a table, once it knows what moved. Over test:er_files` store, where the readings assert Node links to Node and mark Node reaches Node ** with no fact asserted of it, the readings` fact types that keep a table (compile:kt_rleft, of an operand holding that store, M moved and the readings` facts compile:ip_r1 reads) are M alone: Node links to Node, whose facts the readings assert (the tenth place holds them) but which did not move and which nothing derives, is not among them, nor Node reaches Node, marked derived but asserted of nothing; and over law-kt-left.db, whose _derived holds a fact of D, the ledger`s (compile:kt_ledger) are D and M. So a table storing Node links to Node alone is left (compile:kt_ok2), and is read once Node links to Node moved. The database is made fresh before and cleared after. Run first with compile:kt_rleft answering every fact type the readings assert, as the read took them before, it failed (kt-left -> F).",
