"test:eng_recursive holds that a stored derived fact type whose rule reads the derived fact type itself is read as its rules, to the least fixpoint, in SQL. One literal readings file: Node links to Node is asserted (a to b, b to c, c to d, x to y), and Node reaches Node is marked ** and derived by two rules, the links themselves and Node1 reaches Node3 iff Node1 reaches Node2 and Node2 reaches Node3, the non-linear form core.md gives Domain reaches Domain. A ** fact type is derived on update, which nothing does, so it is read as its rules and has no table, and one no Function yields is a view. The store compile:check makes is laid out in law-eng-recursive.db and filled as a compile fills it (test:dv_s2, test:dv_s3), and the script creates a view of Node reaches Node, read as test:recursive_view reads the * one (test:rv_s4), whose rows are the seven of the closure: a reaches b, c and d, b reaches c and d, c reaches d, and x reaches y. The database is cleared after. The engine`s plan (compile:eng_plan) plans no derived fact type, so the rows are the view`s and no table`s.",
