"test:recursive_view holds that a derived fact type computed on read whose rules read it is a view, its rows the least fixpoint, by SQLite`s WITH RECURSIVE. The readings of test:er_files with Node reaches Node marked * instead of **: the relational map lays out no table for the derived fact type, the script creates a view of it, and the view answers the seven rows of the closure. SQLite takes the recursive table once in a select and never inside a subquery, so the rule Node1 reaches Node3 iff Node1 reaches Node2 and Node2 reaches Node3, which reads the derived fact type twice, is said once for each rule that reads it not at all, the derived fact type joined to that rule`s select, the same least fixpoint (a transitive closure is the closure of its base). The database is law-recursive-view.db, made fresh before and cleared after. Run first, the derived fact type was no view, since a view was no derived fact type that reads itself, and it failed.",
