"test:reflect_sql holds that each instance arm`s SQL writes, for the instances a write touched, what store:refl_new adds for that arm. The literal store is the composed store with a write: law-rs-dc an instance of Domain Change no event moved, which has no machine and stands at Proposed, derived (status is semi-derived); law-rs-dc2 one whose machine is stored at Under Review, as a step leaves a machine an event moved; and law-rs-v an instance of the value type Design Note, which belongs to no Domain. The oracle is store:refl_new over that store, each instance arm`s cell, and its rows naming those instances or their machines. The SQL is the program storage:refl_program answers, run through sqlite:scratch over tables laid out in a literal layout of each kind -- a relation (Cls, Sub, Eff) and absorbed columns of Fn keyed first or second -- filled with the composed store`s rows of each fact type it reads, then the steps before the write, the write`s rows, and the steps after: the derived fact type`s rows naming those instances are the oracle`s, for each of the seven arms. Run first, before the program existed, it failed. Nothing files Function belongs to Domain for an instance, an instance`s Domain being the database it is read from, so the law asks that the oracle`s FunctionBelongsToDomain rows naming the write`s instances be empty.",
