       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rq_oracle"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionBelongsToDomain")), A("id"))))),
       A("test:rq_parts")))),
"test:deep_inherit holds that a fact type its supertype plays is the subtype`s at any depth, as a property a C# superclass declares is its subclasses` (a property is associated across the whole type hierarchy). One literal readings file: Phone is a subtype of Device, Device of Asset, Owner owns Asset, and Owner carries Phone is derived iff Owner owns that Phone, a clause naming Phone where the fact type declares Asset two levels up. The rule must build: Owner carries Phone is among the derived fact types derive:rp_rules answers (rpath`s join reading). Run first, read:rule_narrow_try tried the subtype`s direct supertypes alone (read:rule_supers_of), found Device, which plays no role of Owner owns Asset, and the rule built nothing, the shape csdp.md`s Domain Change touches Table iff that Domain Change proposes some Fact Type had (Fact Type is an Object Type is a Function); it failed.",
DEF("test:deep_inherit",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("OwnerCarriesPhone")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("derive:rp_rules"))),
       S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("inherit.md"), A("Asset(.id) is an entity type.\nOwner(.id) is an entity type.\nDevice is a subtype of Asset.\nPhone is a subtype of Device.\nOwner owns Asset.\n  Each Owner, Asset combination occurs at most once in the population of Owner owns Asset.\nOwner carries Phone. *\n  Each Owner, Phone combination occurs at most once in the population of Owner carries Phone.\n* Owner carries Phone iff Owner owns that Phone.\nOwner 'o1' owns Asset 'p1'.\n"), A("fx/inherit.md"))))))),
"A RULE SENTENCE WITH NO MARKER IS A FULLY DERIVED RULE, AND THE CHECK SAYS SO (no marker reads as * outside strict and is an error under strict). test:unmarked_rule reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does. Support Request has Message, Message mentions Category and Support Request has Category are declared with no marker, and `Support Request has Category if that Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category` carries none either; Message has Category is declared `+` and its rule `Message has Category iff Message mentions Category` carries none. Over what the check answers: state:derived marks Support Request has Category full and Message has Category semi, the declaration`s marker standing; the reader reads Support Request has Category`s rule as a join, among the heads of the store the cells make (derive:rule_heads; the rule reader fills no state:rules, read:state_rules); the fact types are the four declared and no other, so the sentence was not tiled into a fact type named for itself; the findings hold exactly one `unmarked` row, for Support Request has Category, carrying the sentence, reported under the default and refused under strict; and the derivation over the store the cells make answers r1 has billing and nothing else. Run first, before the reader read an unmarked `if` as a rule, it failed: the sentence was a fact type of its own and nothing named it.",
DEF("test:um_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("rules.md"), A("Support Request(.id) is an entity type.\nMessage(.id) is an entity type.\nCategory(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Request has Message.\n  Each Support Request, Message combination occurs at most once in the population of Support Request has Message.\nMessage mentions Category.\n  Each Message, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Message mentions Category.\nSupport Request has Category.\n  Each Support Request, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Support Request has Category.\nMessage has Category. +\n  Each Message, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Message has Category.\nSupport Request has Category if that Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category.\nMessage has Category iff Message mentions Category.\nSupport Request 'r1' has Message 'm1'.\nMessage 'm1' mentions Category 'billing'.\n"), A("fx/rules.md"))))),
"<cells, findings> of test:um_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:um_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:um_files")))),
DEF("test:um_cell",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2))))),
"<kind, <cells, findings>> to the findings of that kind.",
DEF("test:um_found",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1))), S2(A("CONS"), N(2)), K(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("distl"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)))))),
"The status a finding carries: refused under strict, reported under the default.",
DEF("test:um_status",
    S4(A("COND"), A("read:strict"), K(A("refused")), K(A("reported")))),
DEF("test:unmarked_rule",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("SupportRequestHasCategory"), A("full"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:derived")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("MessageHasCategory"), A("semi"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:derived")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("SupportRequestHasCategory")), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:rule_heads"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), N(1))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))), K(S4(A("SupportRequestHasMessage"), A("MessageMentionsCategory"), A("SupportRequestHasCategory"), A("MessageHasCategory"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("unmarked")), A("id"))), S2(A("CONS"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("unmarked")), K(A("SupportRequestHasCategory")), A("test:um_status"), K(PHI()), K(A("Support Request has Category if that Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("SupportRequestHasCategory")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), N(1)))), K(S1(S2(A("r1"), A("billing"))))))),
       A("test:um_run")))),
"A RULE WHOSE DERIVED FACT TYPE OR BODY NAMES NO DECLARED FACT TYPE IS SAID. test:rule_diagnostics reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does. Support Request has Message, Message mentions Category, Message refers to Category and Support Request has Category are declared; `* Support Request has Category iff Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category` names only declared fact types; `* Support Request cites Category iff Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category` derives a derived fact type no reading declares; and `* Message refers to Category iff Message quotes Category` has a condition clause, Message quotes Category, that no reading declares. Over the findings the check answers: exactly one `undeclared_dft` row, for Support Request cites Category, carrying its sentence; exactly one `unresolved` row, for the clause Message quotes Category, carrying the clause and the sentence it is in; each reported under the default and refused under strict. Run first, before the check named either, it failed: the rule with the undeclared derived fact type came to nothing without a word, and the other was only an UNDELIVERED derived fact type whose reason, no form says this condition, named no clause.",
DEF("test:rd_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("rules.md"), A("Support Request(.id) is an entity type.\nMessage(.id) is an entity type.\nCategory(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Request has Message.\n  Each Support Request, Message combination occurs at most once in the population of Support Request has Message.\nMessage mentions Category.\n  Each Message, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Message mentions Category.\nMessage refers to Category.\n  Each Message, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Message refers to Category.\nSupport Request has Category.\n  Each Support Request, Category combination occurs at most once in the population of Support Request has Category.\n* Support Request has Category iff Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category.\n* Support Request cites Category iff Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category.\n* Message refers to Category iff Message quotes Category.\n"), A("fx/rules.md"))))),
"<cells, findings> of test:rd_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:rd_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rd_files")))),
DEF("test:rule_diagnostics",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("undeclared_dft")), A("id"))), S2(A("CONS"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("undeclared_dft")), K(A("SupportRequestCitesCategory")), A("test:um_status"), K(PHI()), K(A("Support Request cites Category iff Support Request has Message and that Message mentions Category")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("unresolved")), A("id"))), S2(A("CONS"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("unresolved")), K(A("Message quotes Category")), A("test:um_status"), K(PHI()), K(A("Message quotes Category (in: Message refers to Category iff Message quotes Category)"))))))),
       A("test:rd_run")))),
"A CONSTRAINT DECIDED BY A PREDICATE NO LISTED DEF DECIDES IS SAID, AND UNDER STRICT IT IS REFUSED. test:unlisted_decider reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does. It declares Constraint is decided by Predicate, Predicate has Module Path and Predicate has Symbol Name as core.md and imports.md do, and binds two Constraints: c-listed to Predicate p-listed, Module Path arest, Symbol Name decide:declared_once, which decide:deciders lists; c-unlisted to Predicate p-unlisted, Module Path arest, Symbol Name decide:not_listed, which it does not. Eight more listed bindings stand before c-unlisted`s, so its rows are the tenth of each population and lie in its second chunk of nine. Over the findings the check answers: exactly one `undecided` row, for c-unlisted, carrying its binding, reported under the default and refused under strict. Run first, before the check read the binding, it failed: cmd:dec_sym answers the empty name for an unlisted Symbol Name, so the constraint was decided by nothing and nothing said so.",
DEF("test:ud_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("deciders.md"), A("Constraint(.id) is an entity type.\nPredicate(.id) is an entity type.\nModule Path is a value type.\nSymbol Name is a value type.\nConstraint is decided by Predicate.\n  Each Constraint is decided by at most one Predicate.\nPredicate has Module Path.\n  Each Predicate has at most one Module Path.\nPredicate has Symbol Name.\n  Each Predicate has at most one Symbol Name.\nConstraint 'c-listed' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nPredicate 'p-listed' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p-listed' has Symbol Name 'decide:declared_once'.\nConstraint 'c1' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c2' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c3' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c4' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c5' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c6' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c7' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nConstraint 'c8' is decided by Predicate 'p-listed'.\nPredicate 'p1' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p2' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p3' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p4' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p5' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p6' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p7' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p8' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p1' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p2' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p3' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p4' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p5' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p6' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p7' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nPredicate 'p8' has Symbol Name 'decide:ssrf'.\nConstraint 'c-unlisted' is decided by Predicate 'p-unlisted'.\nPredicate 'p-unlisted' has Module Path 'arest'.\nPredicate 'p-unlisted' has Symbol Name 'decide:not_listed'.\n"), A("fx/deciders.md"))))),
"<cells, findings> of test:ud_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:ud_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ud_files")))),
DEF("test:unlisted_decider",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S2(A("CONS"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("undecided")), K(A("c-unlisted")), A("test:um_status"), K(PHI()), K(A("Constraint 'c-unlisted' is decided by Predicate 'p-unlisted' (Module Path 'arest', Symbol Name 'decide:not_listed'), which no DEF decide:deciders lists decides")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("undecided")), A("test:ud_run"))))),
"A CONSTRAINT MUST CONSTRAIN A FACT TYPE THAT EXISTS, AND OUTSIDE STRICT THE READER CREATES IT (a constraint constrains one or more fact types, and those fact types must exist; outside strict the reader may create one that is missing). test:created_ft reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does. It declares Widget, Owner and Maker as entity types and Color as a value type, and no fact type. It then states nine constraints whose readings no sentence declares. Three are elementary: `Each Widget belongs to at most one Owner`, `Each Widget is made by exactly one Maker` and `Each Widget has some Color`. Six are not created. `For each Owner, at most one Widget is kept by that Owner` and `Each Widget, Owner combination occurs at most once in the population of Widget is sold to Owner` are split by a comma, and the for-each extraction drops predicate words, so the reading it makes is not the sentence`s. One names Region, which no sentence declares. `at least one`, `at most 2` and `exactly 2` are quantifiers no attach arm reads. Under the default, the check answers these. The fact types are exactly the three the elementary constraints name. Each is played by the declared object types, and each carries what its constraint says: a uniqueness on Widget`s role for belongs to; a uniqueness and a mandatory on Widget`s role for is made by; a mandatory on Widget`s role and the spanning uniqueness for has. The findings hold one `created` row per created fact type, named for it and carrying the constraint`s sentence, reported. The other six stay `unattached`. Under strict, nothing is created: there are no fact types and no `created` rows, and all nine constraints are `unattached`. Run first, before the reader created a fact type, it failed: all nine were unattached and the store held no fact type.",
DEF("test:cf_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("created.md"), A("Widget(.id) is an entity type.\nOwner(.id) is an entity type.\nMaker(.id) is an entity type.\nColor is a value type.\nEach Widget belongs to at most one Owner.\nEach Widget is made by exactly one Maker.\nEach Widget has some Color.\nFor each Owner, at most one Widget is kept by that Owner.\nEach Widget, Owner combination occurs at most once in the population of Widget is sold to Owner.\nEach Widget belongs to at most one Region.\nEach Owner holds at least one Widget.\nEach Widget is listed by at most 2 Owner.\nEach Widget is lent to exactly 2 Owner.\n"), A("fx/created.md"))))),
DEF("test:cf_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:cf_files")))),
"<cells, findings> to the names of the fact types state:fts holds.",
DEF("test:cf_names",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
"<cells, findings> under the default: the three created fact types and no other, each row as a declared reading and its constraint would give it, one created finding each, and the six other constraints unattached.",
DEF("test:cf_default",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S3(A("WidgetBelongsToOwner"), A("WidgetIsMadeByMaker"), A("WidgetHasColor"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"),
          K(S3(S5(A("WidgetBelongsToOwner"), S2(A("Widget"), A("Owner")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("WidgetIsMadeByMaker"), S2(A("Widget"), A("Maker")), S1(S1(N(1))), S1(N(1)), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("WidgetHasColor"), S2(A("Widget"), A("Color")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), S1(N(1)), S1(PHI())))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("created")), A("id"))),
          K(S3(S5(A("created"), A("WidgetBelongsToOwner"), A("reported"), PHI(), A("Each Widget belongs to at most one Owner")),
               S5(A("created"), A("WidgetIsMadeByMaker"), A("reported"), PHI(), A("Each Widget is made by exactly one Maker")),
               S5(A("created"), A("WidgetHasColor"), A("reported"), PHI(), A("Each Widget has some Color")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("unattached")), A("id")))),
          K(S6(A("ForEachOwner,AtMostOneWidgetIsKeptByThatOwner"), A("EachWidget,OwnerCombinationOccursAtMostOnceInThePopulationOfWidgetIsSoldToOwner"), A("EachWidgetBelongsToAtMostOneRegion"), A("EachOwnerHoldsAtLeastOneWidget"), A("EachWidgetIsListedByAtMost2Owner"), A("EachWidgetIsLentToExactly2Owner")))))))),
"<cells, findings> under strict: no fact type, no created finding, and all nine constraints unattached and refused.",
DEF("test:cf_strict",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:cf_names")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("created")), A("id")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("unattached")), A("id")))), K(N(9))))))),
DEF("test:created_ft",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("read:strict"), A("test:cf_strict"), A("test:cf_default")), A("test:cf_run"))),
"ONLY AN ELEMENTARY READING IS CREATED, AND NEVER A SECOND READING OF A FACT TYPE THAT EXISTS. test:created_elem reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does, with the shapes measured on a served app`s check. A reader that created a fact type for every such reading created 23 there, and the store came out alethic_clean F. The SQL judge`s one alethic violation was the mandatory on MessageBelongsToSupportRequestOrToSupportChat, which no Message fills. The file declares the object types and one fact type, Integration has Name. It then states six constraints over readings no sentence declares. Five must not create. `Each Message belongs to exactly one Support Request or to exactly one Support Chat` is a disjunctive mandatory (the grammar`s Disjunction 'or'). `Each Entity List has at most one Page per Page Number` and `Each GitHub Project belongs to at most one Organization with Project Number` are each read by the compact arm as a ternary with a uniqueness on one role, which is not elementary (a uniqueness spans at least n-1 roles). `For each Organization and Project Number, at most one GitHub Project belongs to that Organization with that Project Number` is split by a comma. `Each Name belongs to at most one Integration` reads the fact type Integration has Name the other way round; on that app it created a second fact type over the same two players, and the tables Name and URL. One must create: `Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern`. Under the default, the fact types are Integration has Name and Alert belongs to Error Pattern, the findings hold exactly one `created` row, for Alert belongs to Error Pattern, and five `unattached` rows. Under strict, the fact types are Integration has Name alone, nothing is created, and all six constraints are `unattached`. Run first, before the reader asked for an elementary reading, it failed: all five shapes were created.",
DEF("test:ce_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("elem.md"), A("Message(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Request(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Chat(.id) is an entity type.\nEntity List(.id) is an entity type.\nPage(.id) is an entity type.\nPage Number is a value type.\nGitHub Project(.id) is an entity type.\nOrganization(.id) is an entity type.\nProject Number is a value type.\nIntegration(.id) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\nAlert(.id) is an entity type.\nError Pattern(.id) is an entity type.\nIntegration has Name.\nEach Message belongs to exactly one Support Request or to exactly one Support Chat.\nEach Entity List has at most one Page per Page Number.\nEach GitHub Project belongs to at most one Organization with Project Number.\nFor each Organization and Project Number, at most one GitHub Project belongs to that Organization with that Project Number.\nEach Name belongs to at most one Integration.\nEach Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern.\n"), A("fx/elem.md"))))))),
DEF("test:ce_default",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S2(A("IntegrationHasName"), A("AlertBelongsToErrorPattern"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("created")), A("id"))),
          K(S1(S5(A("created"), A("AlertBelongsToErrorPattern"), A("reported"), PHI(), A("Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S5(A("AlertBelongsToErrorPattern"), S2(A("Alert"), A("Error Pattern")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))))))),
DEF("test:ce_strict",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S1(A("IntegrationHasName"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("created")), A("id"))))))),
"test:no_readings holds that a readings file declaring no fact type still compiles to a schema. One entity type and one constraint whose reading names an undeclared object type, so nothing creates a fact type (test:created_elem): state:readings is empty, and rmap:readrows flattened it while its first element was no atom, taking the first element of an empty sequence -- selector 1 out of range 0, a crash a served app`s check met. The schema is the entity`s table alone. Run first, it threw.",
DEF("test:no_readings",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), A("schema:ddl"), K(A("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Widget\""))),
       S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("nor.md"), A("# nor\n\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\n\nEach Widget belongs to at most one Region.\n"), A("fx/nor.md"))))))),
"test:constraint_undeclared holds that a name only a constraint sentence uses, and no declaration opens, is said UNDECLARED as a reading`s is. The file of test:no_readings: Each Widget belongs to at most one Region, with Region declared nowhere; the constraint attaches to nothing and creates nothing, and the findings must carry an undeclared row naming Region beside its unattached one. Run first, the check said UNATTACHED alone and gave no UNDECLARED row; it failed.",
DEF("test:constraint_undeclared",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Region")), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(4)), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("undeclared")),
       S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair"))),
          K(S1(S3(A("nor.md"), A("# nor\n\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\n\nEach Widget belongs to at most one Region.\n"), A("fx/nor.md"))))))))))),
"test:group_xo holds that `For each Message, exactly one of the following holds: some Support Request has that Message; some Support Chat has that Message.` reads as a disjunctive mandatory over Message`s role in each item`s fact type. The group reader knew only subtype partitions, `that Object Type is an Entity Type; ...`, and cut each item at its `is`: these items have none, and read:group_items selected from an empty list, `selector 1 out of range 0`, a second crash a served app`s check met. Run first, the compile threw.",
DEF("test:group_xo",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("DJ:e:SupportRequestHasMessage#2+SupportChatHasMessage#2")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:djmands")),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("g.md"), A("# g\n\nMessage(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Request(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Chat(.id) is an entity type.\nSupport Request has Message.\nSupport Chat has Message.\nFor each Message, exactly one of the following holds: some Support Request has that Message; some Support Chat has that Message.\n"), A("fx/g.md"))))))))))),
"test:at_least_one holds that `Each Part is in at least one Zone.` over a declared `Part is in Zone` attaches as `some` does, and that a numeric bound, `Each Widget belongs to exactly 2 Region.`, is the one constraint reported unattached: no record carries a frequency bound, so it is said and not dropped. Run first, both were unattached; it failed.",
"test:excl_kinds holds that a subtype exclusion group is read with its kind: over Shape and its three subtypes, `For each Shape, exactly one of the following holds: that Shape is a Circle; that Shape is a Square.` is the XO row and `For each Shape, at most one of the following holds: that Shape is a Square; that Shape is a Triangle.` the XC row, each <id, type, members> with the members at the subtype facts` role 2. No cell held them: state:exclusions holds both as <<child, <1>> ...>, the checker`s scopes, with no kind and no id; run first, it failed.",
DEF("test:excl_kinds",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:exclusion_cons")),
          S5(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("e.md"), A("# e\n\nShape(.id) is an entity type.\nCircle is a subtype of Shape.\nSquare is a subtype of Shape.\nTriangle is a subtype of Shape.\nFor each Shape, exactly one of the following holds:\n    that Shape is a Circle;\n    that Shape is a Square.\nFor each Shape, at most one of the following holds:\n    that Shape is a Square;\n    that Shape is a Triangle.\n"), A("fx/e.md"))))))),
       K(S2(
          S3(A("XO:CircleIsASubtypeOfShape#2+SquareIsASubtypeOfShape#2"), A("XO"), S2(S2(A("CircleIsASubtypeOfShape"), N(2)), S2(A("SquareIsASubtypeOfShape"), N(2)))),
          S3(A("XC:SquareIsASubtypeOfShape#2+TriangleIsASubtypeOfShape#2"), A("XC"), S2(S2(A("SquareIsASubtypeOfShape"), N(2)), S2(A("TriangleIsASubtypeOfShape"), N(2))))))))),
"test:excl_reflected holds the reflection of an exclusion row to literal cells: an XC over three subtype facts is the alethic object <id, XC, Alethic, <<A, 2>>, <<B, 2>>, <<C, 2>>>, and its span records are numbered by sequence 1, 2 and 3, each at position 1, while a two-sequence subset object keeps the records it had, sequence 1 then 2. The reflection read no exclusion row and an object held two sequences; run first, it failed.",
DEF("test:excl_reflected",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:con_raw"), K(S1(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:exclusion_cons"), S1(S1(S3(A("XC:A#2+B#2+C#2"), A("XC"), S3(S2(A("A"), N(2)), S2(A("B"), N(2)), S2(A("C"), N(2)))))))))),
          K(S1(S6(A("XC:A#2+B#2+C#2"), A("XC"), A("Alethic"), S1(S2(A("A"), N(2))), S1(S2(A("B"), N(2))), S1(S2(A("C"), N(2)))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), S3(A("CONS"), N(4), N(5)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:con_recs"), K(S6(A("x"), A("XC"), A("Alethic"), S1(S2(A("A"), N(2))), S1(S2(A("B"), N(2))), S1(S2(A("C"), N(2)))))),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:con_recs"), K(S5(A("s"), A("SS"), A("Alethic"), S2(S2(A("P"), N(1)), S2(A("P"), N(2))), S1(S2(A("Q"), N(1))))))))),
          K(S6(S2(A("A.2"), S2(A("1"), A("1"))), S2(A("B.2"), S2(A("2"), A("1"))), S2(A("C.2"), S2(A("3"), A("1"))), S2(A("P.1"), S2(A("1"), A("1"))), S2(A("P.2"), S2(A("1"), A("2"))), S2(A("Q.1"), S2(A("2"), A("1")))))))))),
"test:hyphen_post holds that a trailing hyphen-bound adjective is read: over `Person was born in Country -native.` and `Person has hidden- Country.`, state:qualifiers holds <PersonWasBornInCountryNative, <, >, <, native>> and <PersonHasHiddenCountry, <, hidden>, <, >>, the leading words and then the trailing ones. read:hyphen_at read only the leading form, so the first fact type had no row; run first, it failed.",
DEF("test:hyphen_post",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:qualifiers")),
          S5(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), K(S1(S3(A("h.md"), A("# h\n\nPerson(.id) is an entity type.\nCountry(.id) is an entity type.\nPerson was born in Country -native.\nPerson has hidden- Country.\n"), A("fx/h.md"))))))),
       K(S2(
          S3(A("PersonWasBornInCountryNative"), S2(A(""), A("")), S2(A(""), A("native"))),
          S3(A("PersonHasHiddenCountry"), S2(A(""), A("hidden")), S2(A(""), A("")))))))),
DEF("test:at_least_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S1(A("Each Widget belongs to exactly 2 Region"))), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(5)), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_found"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("unattached")),
       S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair"))),
          K(S1(S3(A("alo.md"), A("# alo\n\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nRegion(.id) is an entity type.\nPart(.id) is an entity type.\nZone(.id) is an entity type.\n\nWidget belongs to Region.\nPart is in Zone.\n\nEach Widget belongs to exactly 2 Region.\nEach Part is in at least one Zone.\n"), A("fx/alo.md"))))))))))),
"test:check_stamp holds that a check`s stamp moves with every input it is keyed on, and that only an equal stored stamp counts as unchanged. Over literal inputs: a file`s text, its path, the strict cell and lambda`s text each move compile:stamp_of; compile:same_stamp answers T for the stored row that holds the stamp, and F for another stamp and for a store with no row.",
DEF("test:check_stamp",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("y"))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("b.md"), A("x"))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("T"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x"))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("L"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp_of"), K(S3(A("M"), A("F"), S1(S2(A("a.md"), A("x"))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:same_stamp"), K(S2(A("s1"), S1(S2(A("s1"), A("answer")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:same_stamp"), K(S2(A("s1"), S1(S2(A("s2"), A("answer"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:same_stamp"), K(S2(A("s1"), PHI()))))))),
DEF("test:created_elem",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("read:strict"), A("test:ce_strict"), A("test:ce_default")), A("test:ce_run"))),
"<text> to <cells, findings> of one literal readings file, as compile:check answers them for the files it reads.",
DEF("test:ar_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("CONS"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("alt.md")), A("id"), K(A("fx/alt.md")))), A("id"))))),
"<cells, findings> to the cells as a store, each cell as compile:cellify makes it.",
DEF("test:ar_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), N(1))),
"<cells, findings> to T when every finding is the file`s own, that it declares no Domain: nothing was rejected, left unattached, created or refused.",
DEF("test:ar_quiet",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("domain"))))), N(2))),
"ONE FACT TYPE, SEVERAL READINGS, IN ANY ROLE ORDER (that is the intent of a predicate with alternate readings; NORMA too gives one predicate several verbalizations, to put its roles in any order). ORM writes a predicate`s forward and inverse readings with a slash. test:alt_decl reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:created_elem does. It declares Error Pattern and Alert, and `Error Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.`, then Integration has Name and Name belongs to Integration as two sentences without a slash. Over what the check answers: the fact types are ErrorPatternHasAlert, named by its first reading, and the two the unslashed sentences declare, so only the slash declares an alternate reading and two separate sentences stay two fact types; ErrorPatternHasAlert is played by Error Pattern and Alert in that order; the readings the store reflects for it (reflect:readings, FactTypeHasReading) are rErrorPatternHasAlert and rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern; both of its roles are used in the second (reflect:used, RoleIsUsedInReading); and state:altreadings records the second with the role positions it uses, the fact type`s role 2 first and role 1 second. Nothing is rejected, left unattached or created (test:ar_quiet). Run first, before the reader read the slash, it failed: the sentence was one fact type named for both readings, the slash among its words.",
DEF("test:ar_decl_text",
    K(A("Error Pattern(.id) is an entity type.\nAlert(.id) is an entity type.\nIntegration(.id) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\nError Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.\nIntegration has Name.\nName belongs to Integration.\n"))),
DEF("test:alt_decl",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S3(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("IntegrationHasName"), A("NameBelongsToIntegration"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))), K(S2(A("Error Pattern"), A("Alert"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(S2(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("rErrorPatternHasAlert")), S2(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:readings"), A("test:ar_store"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(S2(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert.1"), A("rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern")), S2(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert.2"), A("rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:used"), A("test:ar_store"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern"), S2(N(2), N(1)))), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:altreadings")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:ar_quiet")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_run"), A("test:ar_decl_text")))),
"A CONSTRAINT ATTACHES THROUGH ANY READING OF ITS FACT TYPE. test:alt_attach reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:alt_decl does. It declares five fact types with a slash and constrains each through its second reading, one per elementary form the attach arms read: `Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern` (at most one), `Each Part is in exactly one Widget` (exactly one), `Each Gadget is kept by some Owner` (some), `For each Maker, at most one Tool is built by that Maker` (for each) and `Each Buyer, Item combination occurs at most once in the population of Buyer buys Item from Seller` (spanning). Each constraint must sit on the fact type the first reading names, on the roles the second reading`s players play in it: ErrorPatternHasAlert unique on Alert`s role 2; WidgetHasPart unique and mandatory on Part`s role 2; OwnerKeepsGadget mandatory on Gadget`s role 2, with the spanning uniqueness every population has; MakerBuildsTool unique on Maker`s role 1; SellerSellsItemToBuyer unique on Item and Buyer, roles 2 and 3. The fact types are those five and no other, and nothing is unattached or created, under the default or strict: a constraint over a reading a slash declares finds that reading before the reader`s creation of a missing fact type is asked. And the uniqueness keeps its sentence under the id of the fact type`s role: read:refl_ctexts answers <UC:in:ErrorPatternHasAlert#2, Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern> (test:ar_ctexts), which it answered for no alternate reading before read:tx_cctx took the alternate records. Run first, it failed: the arms matched each constraint to the alternate reading`s record, which no fact type reads, so nothing was unattached and every fact type kept only its spanning default.",
DEF("test:ar_attach_text",
    K(A("Error Pattern(.id) is an entity type.\nAlert(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nPart(.id) is an entity type.\nOwner(.id) is an entity type.\nGadget(.id) is an entity type.\nMaker(.id) is an entity type.\nTool(.id) is an entity type.\nSeller(.id) is an entity type.\nBuyer(.id) is an entity type.\nItem(.id) is an entity type.\nError Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.\nEach Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern.\nWidget has Part / Part is in Widget.\nEach Part is in exactly one Widget.\nOwner keeps Gadget / Gadget is kept by Owner.\nEach Gadget is kept by some Owner.\nMaker builds Tool / Tool is built by Maker.\nFor each Maker, at most one Tool is built by that Maker.\nSeller sells Item to Buyer / Buyer buys Item from Seller.\nEach Buyer, Item combination occurs at most once in the population of Buyer buys Item from Seller.\n"))),
"The <constraint id, sentence> rows read:refl_ctexts reflects for test:ar_attach_text`s sentences (ConstraintHasText).",
DEF("test:ar_ctexts",
    S5(A("COMP"), A("read:refl_ctexts"), N(1), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("CONS"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("alt.md")), A("id"), K(A("fx/alt.md")))), A("test:ar_attach_text"))))),
DEF("test:alt_attach",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("UC:in:ErrorPatternHasAlert#2"), A("Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern"))), A("test:ar_ctexts"))),
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S5(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("WidgetHasPart"), A("OwnerKeepsGadget"), A("MakerBuildsTool"), A("SellerSellsItemToBuyer"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"),
          K(S5(S5(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), S2(A("Error Pattern"), A("Alert")), S1(S1(N(2))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("WidgetHasPart"), S2(A("Widget"), A("Part")), S1(S1(N(2))), S1(N(2)), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("OwnerKeepsGadget"), S2(A("Owner"), A("Gadget")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), S1(N(2)), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("MakerBuildsTool"), S2(A("Maker"), A("Tool")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
               S5(A("SellerSellsItemToBuyer"), S3(A("Seller"), A("Item"), A("Buyer")), S1(S2(N(2), N(3))), PHI(), S1(PHI())))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:ar_quiet")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_run"), A("test:ar_attach_text")))))),
"AN INSTANCE FACT IN ANY READING ASSERTS THE SAME FACT. test:alt_instance reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:alt_decl does. It declares `Error Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.` and `Seller sells Item to Buyer / Buyer buys Item from Seller.`, and states `Error Pattern 'e0' has Alert 'a0'.`, `Alert 'a1' belongs to Error Pattern 'e1'.` and `Buyer 'b1' buys Item 'i1' from Seller 's1'.`. The population of ErrorPatternHasAlert must be the rows <e0, a0> and <e1, a1>, and that of SellerSellsItemToBuyer the row <s1, i1, b1>: each row in the fact type`s role order, whichever reading stated it. Nothing is rejected, and each instance is filed under its type (read:refl_instances, ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType): a1 an Alert, e1 an Error Pattern, b1 a Buyer, s1 a Seller. Run first, before an instance sentence was matched against the alternate readings, it failed: the three sentences in the second reading were rejected as matching no reading.",
DEF("test:ar_inst_text",
    K(A("Error Pattern(.id) is an entity type.\nAlert(.id) is an entity type.\nSeller(.id) is an entity type.\nBuyer(.id) is an entity type.\nItem(.id) is an entity type.\nError Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.\nSeller sells Item to Buyer / Buyer buys Item from Seller.\nError Pattern 'e0' has Alert 'a0'.\nAlert 'a1' belongs to Error Pattern 'e1'.\nBuyer 'b1' buys Item 'i1' from Seller 's1'.\n"))),
"<name, <cells, findings>> to the rows of that fact type`s population in state:fts.",
DEF("test:ar_pop",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1))), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), N(5), N(2)), K(PHI()))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("distl"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), N(2))))))),
DEF("test:ar_insts",
    S5(A("COMP"), A("read:refl_instances"), N(1), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("CONS"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("alt.md")), A("id"), K(A("fx/alt.md")))), A("test:ar_inst_text"))))),
DEF("test:alt_instance",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(S2(A("a1"), A("Alert")), S2(A("e1"), A("Error Pattern")), S2(A("b1"), A("Buyer")), S2(A("s1"), A("Seller")))), A("test:ar_insts")))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("e0"), A("a0")), S2(A("e1"), A("a1")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("SellerSellsItemToBuyer")), A("id"))), K(S1(S3(A("s1"), A("i1"), A("b1")))))),
          A("test:ar_quiet")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_run"), A("test:ar_inst_text")))))),
"THE SHORT FORM NAMES EACH PLAYER ONCE. NORMA writes a binary`s two readings as `Error Pattern has / belongs to Alert`: the first player, the forward predicate, a slash, the inverse predicate, the second player. test:alt_short reads `Error Pattern has / belongs to Alert.`, `Each Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern.` and `Alert 'a1' belongs to Error Pattern 'e1'.` through compile:check, as test:alt_decl does. It must read as the long form `Error Pattern has Alert / Alert belongs to Error Pattern.` reads: the one fact type ErrorPatternHasAlert over Error Pattern and Alert, unique on role 2, its population the row <e1, a1>; state:altreadings records rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern at positions 2 and 1; nothing is rejected, unattached or created. Run first, before the reader read the short form, it failed: neither half names both players, so the slash was not taken and the sentence was a fact type of its own.",
DEF("test:ar_short_text",
    K(A("Error Pattern(.id) is an entity type.\nAlert(.id) is an entity type.\nError Pattern has / belongs to Alert.\nEach Alert belongs to at most one Error Pattern.\nAlert 'a1' belongs to Error Pattern 'e1'.\n"))),
DEF("test:alt_short",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S6(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:cf_names"), K(S1(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S5(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), S2(A("Error Pattern"), A("Alert")), S1(S1(N(2))), PHI(), S1(S1(S2(A("e1"), A("a1")))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert"), A("rAlertBelongsToErrorPattern"), S2(N(2), N(1)))), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:um_cell"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:altreadings")), A("id")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ErrorPatternHasAlert")), A("id"))), K(S1(S2(A("e1"), A("a1")))))),
       A("test:ar_quiet")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ar_run"), A("test:ar_short_text")))),
"EVERY DERIVED FACT TYPE IS READ IN SQL AS THE CLOSURE ANSWERS IT. test:derive_sql reads one literal readings file through compile:check (test:dq_files), as test:derived_view does: Member joins Club, Club holds Venue and Node links to Node are asserted; Member attends Venue is marked * and joins the two; Club seats Member is marked ** and is Member joins Club turned round; Member has Grade is marked +, Grade gold for each Member who joins some Club, and bob is entered silver and dee bronze; Club favors Venue is marked ++, Club holds Venue beside the entered go favors ely; Node reaches Node is marked * and is the closure of Node links to Node; Node trails Node is marked + and has one rule, which reads it (Node1 trails Node3 if Node1 trails Node2 and Node2 links to Node3), and a trails b is entered, so the chain starts from what was entered: a trails b, c and d; Node shadows Node is marked * and has one rule, which reads it, and nothing seeds it, so it derives nothing; Member is idle is marked * and is each Member with some Grade who attends no Venue, a negation over two derived fact types computed on read; Member likes Venue is marked + and is Member attends Venue beside the entered dee likes ely; and Venue is run by Club is marked * and is Club holds Venue read backwards under Each Venue is run by at most one Club, so york, which two Clubs hold, is run by none. The store is closed as a compile closes it (compile:close_store) and laid out in law-derive-sql.db as a compile lays it out (storage:schema, compile:tables), and the engine computes the derived fact types it takes (compile:eng_plan, storage:derive_dft). For each of the ten derived fact types, the rows the database answers where schema:read_place says the derived fact type is read, over the env with its reads (schema:rd_env), are the rows derive:closed answers for it over the store as its readings assert it. The database is made fresh before and cleared after. Run first, before a derived fact type computed on read had a place SQL reads it at, it failed (unresolved atom schema:rd_env). Run again with Node trails Node and Node shadows Node, before a recursion was seeded by what was entered, it threw selector 1 out of range 0 (sqlite:dft_sql of no recipes, under sqlite:vw_place), as a served app`s compile did; seeded but with the mode read off the wrong operand, Node trails Node answered a trails b alone, and it failed.",
DEF("test:dq_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("heads.md"), A("Member(.id) is an entity type.\nClub(.id) is an entity type.\nVenue(.id) is an entity type.\nNode(.id) is an entity type.\nGrade is a value type.\nMember joins Club.\n  Each Member, Club combination occurs at most once in the population of Member joins Club.\nClub holds Venue.\n  Each Club, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Club holds Venue.\nNode links to Node.\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node links to Node.\nMember attends Venue. *\n  Each Member, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Member attends Venue.\n* Member attends Venue iff Member joins Club and that Club holds Venue.\nClub seats Member. **\n  Each Club, Member combination occurs at most once in the population of Club seats Member.\n** Club seats Member iff Member joins that Club.\nMember has Grade. +\n  Each Member has at most one Grade.\n+ Member has Grade 'gold' if that Member joins some Club.\nClub favors Venue. ++\n  Each Club, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Club favors Venue.\n++ Club favors Venue if Club holds Venue.\nNode reaches Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node reaches Node.\n* Node1 reaches Node2 iff Node1 links to Node2.\n* Node1 reaches Node3 iff Node1 reaches Node2 and Node2 reaches Node3.\nNode trails Node. +\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node trails Node.\n+ Node1 trails Node3 if Node1 trails Node2 and Node2 links to Node3.\nNode shadows Node. *\n  Each Node, Node combination occurs at most once in the population of Node shadows Node.\n* Node1 shadows Node3 iff Node1 shadows Node2 and Node2 links to Node3.\nMember is idle. *\n* Member is idle iff Member has some Grade and it is not true that that Member attends some Venue.\nMember likes Venue. +\n  Each Member, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Member likes Venue.\n+ Member likes Venue if Member attends Venue.\nVenue is run by Club. *\n  Each Venue is run by at most one Club.\n* Venue is run by Club iff Club holds that Venue.\nMember 'ann' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'cy' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'bob' joins Club 'go'.\nMember 'bob' has Grade 'silver'.\nMember 'dee' has Grade 'bronze'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'york'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'leeds'.\nClub 'go' holds Venue 'hull'.\nClub 'go' holds Venue 'york'.\nClub 'rowing' holds Venue 'ely'.\nClub 'go' favors Venue 'ely'.\nMember 'dee' likes Venue 'ely'.\nNode 'a' links to Node 'b'.\nNode 'b' links to Node 'c'.\nNode 'c' links to Node 'd'.\nNode 'x' links to Node 'y'.\nNode 'a' trails Node 'b'.\n"), A("fx/heads.md"))))),
"The cells compile:check answers for test:dq_files, each chunked as a compile files it; test:dq_store, those filed.",
DEF("test:dq_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:dq_files"))),
DEF("test:dq_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), A("test:dq_cells"))),
DEF("test:dq_dfts",
