       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:dq_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dq_dfts"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), A("schema:rd_env"), A("schema:env"), N(1)), A("test:dq_store"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
DEF("test:derive_sql",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:dq_verdict"), A("test:dq_eng"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), A("test:dq_s1"))),
"test:rkeep_scope holds main:w2_rkeep, which deontic and set-comparison rows a write`s validation asks again, to the players of the fact types a row names. The row is the composed store`s deontic mandatory over Constraint Span (DEO:m:ConstraintIsInvolvedInConstraintSpan#1), whose players are Constraint and Role. A write that moved the instances of Status alone, and no population the row names, cannot move what it answers: F. One that moved the instances of Ring Constraint, a subtype of Constraint, can: T; and so can one that moved Constraint Span itself: T. Run first, main:w2_rkeep kept every row when a write moved any type`s instances, which every create does, and the write that moved Status alone kept it: F.",
DEF("test:rk_row",
    K(S3(A("DEO:m:ConstraintIsInvolvedInConstraintSpan#1"), A("mandatory"), S1(S2(A("ConstraintSpan"), N(1)))))),
