       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("main:w2_rkeep"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rk_row"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(S1(A("Status")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("main:w2_rkeep"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rk_row"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(PHI()), K(S1(A("Ring Constraint")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("main:w2_rkeep"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rk_row"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("ConstraintSpan"))), K(PHI()))))))),
"THE READ VERBS ANSWER FROM THE DATABASE WHAT THE STORE IN MEMORY ANSWERS. test:query_sql reads test:derive_sql`s readings (test:dq_files) and the fact types orient reads (test:qs_files) through compile:check, closes the store as a compile closes it, lays it out in law-query-sql.db as a compile lays it out and has the engine compute the derived fact types it takes (test:dv_s2, test:dv_s3, test:dq_eng): Member joins Club, Club holds Venue and Node links to Node asserted; Club seats Member and Club favors Venue derived and stored; Member attends Venue, Node reaches Node, Member is idle and Venue is run by Club computed on read; Member has Grade and Member likes Venue semi-derived. The store in memory is the one a server holds of that database, every table read back whole and unprojected as a start reads it (test:qs_back); the store served from the database is those cells beside state:store_db naming it. For each probe -- query over every recipe form, over stored fact types, a stored derived one and ones computed on read, a count read back as an integer and a pairwith of a number; get of an entity with links (bob, chess, york) and of an id that is none; nav; orient of a Domain, of an App and of a name that is neither -- the text system:show answers over the served store is the text it answers over the store in memory, byte for byte. And the database answers each recipe test:qs_sql lists (query:places is no #) and places the stored fact types get and orient cut there (store:places), so the comparison is of the database`s answer with lambda`s and not of lambda with itself; a starts, a sum, a calc, a flat and a sel of a number in a column of text (test:qs_mem) are evaluated in lambda over both. The database is made fresh before and cleared after. Run first, before query took the cells and read the database, it failed.",
DEF("test:qs_db",
    K(A("law-query-sql.db"))),
"AND WHAT orient READS, as the metamodel says it, beside test:dq_files: Domain heads contains clubs, and Domain reaches Domain is computed on read as the closure of containment; each has a Description (Function has Description); App hub has navigable Domain heads; bob, chess and york are required orientation, and york is currently in Status Closed, which is terminal in State Machine Definition Venue. Object Type Instance belongs to Domain is entered of each, but an instance`s Domain is its type`s and these files declare no Domain, so orient answers the Descriptions alone; test:orient_served holds the required leg.",
DEF("test:qs_files",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dq_files"), K(S1(S3(A("orient.md"), A("Domain(.Name) is an entity type.\nApp(.Name) is an entity type.\nFunction(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nStatus(.Name) is an entity type.\nState Machine Definition(.Name) is an entity type.\nDescription is a value type.\nDomain contains Domain.\n  Each Domain, Domain combination occurs at most once in the population of Domain contains Domain.\nDomain reaches Domain. *\n  Each Domain, Domain combination occurs at most once in the population of Domain reaches Domain.\n* Domain1 reaches Domain2 iff Domain1 contains Domain2.\n* Domain1 reaches Domain3 iff Domain1 reaches Domain2 and Domain2 reaches Domain3.\nFunction has Description.\n  Each Function has at most one Description.\nApp has navigable Domain.\n  Each App, Domain combination occurs at most once in the population of App has navigable Domain.\nObject Type Instance belongs to Domain.\n  Each Object Type Instance, Domain combination occurs at most once in the population of Object Type Instance belongs to Domain.\nObject Type Instance is required orientation.\nObject Type Instance is currently in Status.\n  Each Object Type Instance, Status combination occurs at most once in the population of Object Type Instance is currently in Status.\nStatus is terminal in State Machine Definition.\n  Each Status, State Machine Definition combination occurs at most once in the population of Status is terminal in State Machine Definition.\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\n  Each Object Type Instance, Object Type combination occurs at most once in the population of Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nDomain 'heads' contains Domain 'clubs'.\nFunction 'heads' has Description 'Members, clubs and the venues they meet at'.\nFunction 'clubs' has Description 'Clubs and what they hold'.\nApp 'hub' has navigable Domain 'heads'.\nObject Type Instance 'bob' belongs to Domain 'clubs'.\nObject Type Instance 'chess' belongs to Domain 'heads'.\nObject Type Instance 'york' belongs to Domain 'clubs'.\nObject Type Instance 'bob' is required orientation.\nObject Type Instance 'chess' is required orientation.\nObject Type Instance 'york' is required orientation.\nObject Type Instance 'york' is currently in Status 'Closed'.\nStatus 'Closed' is terminal in State Machine Definition 'Venue'.\nObject Type Instance 'heads' is instance of Object Type 'Domain'.\nObject Type Instance 'clubs' is instance of Object Type 'Domain'.\n"), A("fx/orient.md"))))))),
DEF("test:qs_cells",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:qs_files"))),
"<anything> to <the store closed as a compile closes it, the database made fresh>.",
DEF("test:qs_s1",
    S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:close_store"), A("test:qs_cells")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), A("test:qs_db")))),
