"A MANDATORY OVER AN OPEN WORLD IS NOT REFUTED BY ABSENCE. Two stores compiled from one reading: Customer `c1` has an Email and authenticates via no OAuth Account, under `Each Customer authenticates via some OAuth Account.`; one store says OAuth Account`s World Assumption is open, the other closed. Closed, the in-memory judge (cmd:mand_viols) reports c1 and the SQL plan (check:plan) has an entry for the mandatory; open, neither does. Run first, the open store reported c1 as the closed one does.",
"AN EVENT NEED NOT HAVE OCCURRED AT A KNOWN TIME (an event depends on its order, not necessarily on a timestamp). The base store`s Event occurred at Timestamp keeps its uniqueness, at most one Timestamp for an Event, and has no mandatory position: an Event, and so a Fact a reading declares, is not refused for having none. Over the carriers before the change it answered F, the mandatory being there.",
DEF("test:event_untimed",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("atom"), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), N(4)), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), N(3))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:find_desc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("EventOccurredAtTimestamp")), A("store:fts"))))),
"A FACT IS OF THE EVENT TYPE ITS FACT TYPE IS. A Fact is an Event and a Fact Type is an Event Type, so the base store marks Event is of Event Type + and derives it for a Fact from the Fact Type the Fact is of: an Event that is not a Fact has its Event Type entered, and a Fact a reading declares is not refused for having none. Two halves: the base store computes it on read with its entries (derive:semi_dfts), and a store that declares the types as instances.md does, Fact is of Fact Type before Event is of Event Type, reads f1`s Event Type, its Fact Type, beside e1`s entered one. Over the carriers and lambda before the change both answered F: the fact type was not marked, and no arm built the rule, so a Fact had no Event Type. Declared the other way round the fixture answered T without any rule: the instance `Fact f1 is of Fact Type PersonDied` was read into Event is of Event Type itself, so the order is the one instances.md has.",
DEF("test:etd_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("et.md"), A("Function(.Name) is an entity type.\nEvent Type is an entity type.\n  Event Type is a subtype of Function.\nFact Type is an entity type.\n  Fact Type is a subtype of Event Type.\nEvent is an entity type.\n  Event is a subtype of Function.\nFact is an entity type.\n  Fact is a subtype of Event.\nFact is of Fact Type.\n  Each Fact is of exactly one Fact Type.\nEvent is of Event Type. +\n  Each Event is of exactly one Event Type.\n+ Event is of Event Type if that Event is some Fact that is of some Fact Type that is that Event Type.\nFact 'f1' is of Fact Type 'PersonDied'.\nEvent 'e1' is of Event Type 'Signal'.\n"), A("fx/et.md"))))),
DEF("test:etd_rows",
    S9(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("EventIsOfEventType")), A("id")), A("compile:close_store"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:etd_files"))),
