    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("EventIsOfEventType")), A("derive:semi_dfts"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:etd_rows"), K(S2(S2(A("e1"), A("Signal")), S2(A("f1"), A("PersonDied"))))))))),
"A DERIVATION RULE IS NOT MADE TO RESTATE ITS ROLES (a derivation rule is a constraint type, so redeclaring its role relations by hand is wrong). A constraint`s spans already say which roles a derivation reads and which it fills, so the base store`s Derivation Rule has Antecedent Clause carries no mandatory on the Derivation Rule`s role; its uniqueness stands, and an Antecedent Clause still belongs to exactly one Derivation Rule. Over the carriers before the change it answered F.",
"<name, store> to T when the store`s descriptor of the name carries a uniqueness and its first role, the Derivation Rule`s, is not among its mandatory positions.",
DEF("test:no_mand",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("atom"), K(A("F")), S4(A("COND"), A("null"), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(N(1)), N(4))), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), N(3)))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:find_desc"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:fts"), N(2)))))),
"test:set_comparison holds that over the base the derived Set Comparison Constraints are exactly the Constraints of Constraint Type SS, XC or EQ (Halpin ch. 6; NORMA SetComparisonConstraint), some there are, and none is an exclusive-or or an inclusive-or, which are disjunctive mandatories (core.md). Over the rule by the family 'set-comparison' it failed, the XO and OR constraints among them and the subsets and equalities not.",
"THE VERBALIZER SPEAKS A CONSTRAINT AS NORMA DOES (AREST.tex prop:spec; Halpin and Curland, Automated Verbalization for ORM 2). Over the composed base store, the external uniqueness over Column belongs to Table and Column has Name verbalizes in the positive form as the paper`s pattern for a uniqueness no reading opens with: For each A and B, at most one C R that A and S that B. With no verbalize cell this throws.",
DEF("test:vz_external",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("vz:verbalize"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("UC:en:ColumnBelongsToTable#2+ColumnHasName#2")), K(A("positive")))), K(A("For each Table and Name, at most one Column belongs to that Table and has that Name."))))),
"AND EVERY CONSTRAINT A PATTERN COVERS IS SPOKEN. Over the composed base store, each constraint whose fact types all have a primary reading and whose Constraint Type some Verbalization Pattern verbalizes answers a non-empty verbalization in the positive form. A constraint over a fact type with no reading (an objectification`s involvement link) has nothing to read from, and a Constraint Type no pattern names is a pattern to add, so neither is counted here. With no verbalize cell this throws.",
DEF("test:vz_covered",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:vz_unspoken"), A("vz:ctx"))),
"<ctx> to the constraints a pattern covers that verbalize to nothing.",
DEF("test:vz_unspoken",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(4), K(A("T")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(3), K(A("")))), N(5))))), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)), K(PHI()))), S2(A("ALPHA"), S6(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("vz:con"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), K(A("positive")))), S4(A("COND"), S5(A("COMP"), A("vz:legs_read"), N(4), A("vz:crec"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2))), K(A("T")), K(A("F"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2))), N(6), N(1)))))), A("distl"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), N(1)))),
DEF("test:set_comparison",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("test:sc_derived")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sc_derived"), A("test:sc_typed")))))),
