         S3(A("clubs"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("Members and the venues their clubs hold"))))),
"<store in memory, served store> to T when the served store is one a read is answered over (store:served), every probe answers the same text over both (test:qs_same), and orient of heads over the served store answers test:os_heads.",
DEF("test:os_ok",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:served"), N(2)),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:qs_same")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:os_probes"), A("id")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3))), A("orient"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("heads")), N(2))), A("test:os_heads")))))),
"<store, database> to the verdict, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:os_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:os_ok"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:qs_back"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:for_read"), A("test:ss_served")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2))))),
"THE ORIENT HOIST HOLDS THE ANSWER. orient reads the retired once and hands them to each Domain, reads a population with no place once, reads a Domain`s scope once for both its legs, and reads no types where no instance is live. Each test holds the hoisted cell equal to the form it replaced, over test:or_store`s literal rows, and each failed once against a lambda whose hoisted cell was mutated: test:orient_retired_once (with_retired handing each Domain no retired: or-n2, retired by applied, came back), test:orient_rows_once (the values of the set taken in reverse, so not in the set`s order: or-n1`s row first), test:orient_scope_once (each Domain`s scope taken as the Domain alone: or-beta`s Description lost), test:orient_rb_skip (the skip taken where instances are live: no rows).",
"orient on or-app, the retired read once, against each Domain`s parts with the retired read for that Domain.",
DEF("test:orient_retired_once",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("orient"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("or-app")), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("orient:rows"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("orient:parts"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("orient:retired"), N(2))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("or-alpha"), A("or-beta"))), A("id")))))),
       A("test:or_store"))),
"<cells> to <<Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type, 1>, <or-n3, or-n1>, cells>: two values of the set, the second of them first in the population.",
