"AND A WRITE THAT LANDS WHILE A SERVER FRESHENS IS STILL SEEN. A serving host asked whether its store moved, read again what it had read of it, and only then recorded the version, asked a second time: a row another connection committed between the two asks was in the version recorded and in none of what was read, so the server answered without it until some later write moved the store again. And after a write of its own it recorded the version when the request ended, so a row another connection committed between that write`s commit and the request`s end was taken for its own. store:freshen answers whether the store moved and the version it moved to, read ONCE, and the host records that version, the one read before it read anything again. test:fresh_race serves test:query_sql`s fixture from law-fresh-race.db, its version recorded. Another connection puts eve in chess: store:freshen answers T and the version. Another puts dan in chess, after that ask, as a write lands while a server reads again; the store noted at the version store:freshen answered still reads as stale, and once noted at the version a second store:freshen answers, it does not. And store:commit_note is what a server records at a commit of its own: <recorded, the version before the commit, the version after> to the version after where nothing moved the store since it was recorded, and to the version recorded where something did, so the next request reads the store again. The database is cleared after. Run first, before store:freshen was defined, it failed.",
DEF("test:fr_db",
    K(A("law-fresh-race.db"))),
