    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Object Type Instance")), S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:anc_of"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), N(2))))), S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))), K(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("EntityTypeHasReferenceMode")), A("id"))), A("id"))))),
"A RULE READS A FACT BY ANY OF ITS READINGS, AND A NEGATION INSIDE A NEGATION KEEPS WHAT IT SHARES WITH THE ROWS OUTSIDE (Halpin`s universal said as a negated existential, Curland, Halpin and Stirewalt, A Role Calculus for ORM). test:alt_universal reads one file twice, once with `Constraint Span objectifies \"Constraint spans Role\"` and once without: Fact Type has Role, Constraint spans Role / Role is spanned by Constraint, Constraint is of Constraint Type, and Fact Type is covered by Constraint iff that Fact Type has some Role and some Constraint spans that Role and that Constraint is of Constraint Type `UC` and no Role of that Fact Type is not spanned by that Constraint, the last clause said by the passive reading. f1 has roles f1.1 and f1.2, both spanned by u1, and f1.1 by u3 as well; f2 has f2.1 and f2.2, only f2.1 spanned by u2. Only u1 covers its fact type, so the rows are <f1, u1>, objectified or not. Run first, the passive clause read to no fact type and the rule to #; with the passive reading indexed, u3 covered f1 too, the inner negation having anti-joined each role on the roles some constraint spans, any constraint; and over the objectified file the second reading was filed on ConstraintSpansRole, which no record holds.",
DEF("test:alt_universal_files",
    K(S2(S1(S3(A("cover.md"), A("Fact Type(.id) is an entity type.\nRole(.id) is an entity type.\nConstraint(.id) is an entity type.\nConstraint Type is a value type.\nFact Type has Role.\n  Each Role is of at most one Fact Type.\nConstraint spans Role / Role is spanned by Constraint.\n  Each Constraint, Role combination occurs at most once in the population of Constraint spans Role.\nConstraint is of Constraint Type.\n  Each Constraint is of at most one Constraint Type.\nFact Type is covered by Constraint. *\n* Fact Type is covered by Constraint iff that Fact Type has some Role and some Constraint spans that Role and that Constraint is of Constraint Type 'UC' and no Role of that Fact Type is not spanned by that Constraint.\nFact Type 'f1' has Role 'f1.1'.\nFact Type 'f1' has Role 'f1.2'.\nFact Type 'f2' has Role 'f2.1'.\nFact Type 'f2' has Role 'f2.2'.\nConstraint 'u1' spans Role 'f1.1'.\nConstraint 'u1' spans Role 'f1.2'.\nConstraint 'u2' spans Role 'f2.1'.\nConstraint 'u3' spans Role 'f1.1'.\nConstraint 'u1' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\nConstraint 'u2' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\nConstraint 'u3' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\n"), A("cover/cover.md"))), S1(S3(A("cover.md"), A("Fact Type(.id) is an entity type.\nRole(.id) is an entity type.\nConstraint(.id) is an entity type.\nConstraint Type is a value type.\nFact Type has Role.\n  Each Role is of at most one Fact Type.\nConstraint spans Role / Role is spanned by Constraint.\n  Each Constraint, Role combination occurs at most once in the population of Constraint spans Role.\nConstraint is of Constraint Type.\n  Each Constraint is of at most one Constraint Type.\nConstraint Span objectifies \"Constraint spans Role\".\nFact Type is covered by Constraint. *\n* Fact Type is covered by Constraint iff that Fact Type has some Role and some Constraint spans that Role and that Constraint is of Constraint Type 'UC' and no Role of that Fact Type is not spanned by that Constraint.\nFact Type 'f1' has Role 'f1.1'.\nFact Type 'f1' has Role 'f1.2'.\nFact Type 'f2' has Role 'f2.1'.\nFact Type 'f2' has Role 'f2.2'.\nConstraint 'u1' spans Role 'f1.1'.\nConstraint 'u1' spans Role 'f1.2'.\nConstraint 'u2' spans Role 'f2.1'.\nConstraint 'u3' spans Role 'f1.1'.\nConstraint 'u1' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\nConstraint 'u2' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\nConstraint 'u3' is of Constraint Type 'UC'.\n"), A("cover/cover.md")))))),
DEF("test:alt_universal_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FactTypeIsCoveredByConstraint")), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:filed"), S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("id")))))),
DEF("test:alt_universal",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:alt_universal_rows"), K(S1(S2(A("f1"), A("u1"))))))), A("test:alt_universal_files"))),
"THE OBJECTIFICATIONS THE READER READ ARE THE STORE`S FACTS (core.md, Object Type objectifies Fact Type and Fact Type is implicitly objectified, NORMA`s Objectification and its IsImplied). test:nests_filed holds the booted store to its own cells: the rows of Object Type objectifies Fact Type are the pairs state:nestings holds, as a set; some fact type is implicitly objectified; and every one that is is a nest. Run first, before read:reflect filed them, the store held no row of either and it answered F.",
