    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("read:name_sorted"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("implode"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A(" ")), A("id")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:eval"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("proj"), A("ObjectTypeObjectifiesFactType"), S2(N(1), N(2)))), A("derive:store_pairs"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("read:name_sorted"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), A("implode"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A(" ")), A("id")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:cellrows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:nestings")), A("id"))))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:eval"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("proj"), A("FactTypeIsImplicitlyObjectified"), S1(N(1)))), A("derive:store_pairs")))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:eval"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("proj"), A("FactTypeIsImplicitlyObjectified"), S1(N(1)))), A("derive:store_pairs")))), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:cellrows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:nestings")), A("id")))))))),
       A("id"))),
"THE INDEPENDENCE NORMA SETS IS THE RULE`S (core.md, Object Type is independent: an implied objectification whose one uniqueness spans every role, its universal said as a negated existential). test:independent_derived holds the rule`s rows over the booted store to the reader`s own independent object types (rmap:otindep, what the relational map makes concept types of): the same names, and some. Run first, before a nest`s uniqueness was a Constraint of the store, the rule derived no row and it answered F.",
